      "narrative": "AheadComputing is a seed-stage semiconductor company founded by Debbie Marr, Mark Dechene, Jonathan Pearce, and Srikanth Srinivasan that has raised $51.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 11 private and public companies in the Chips & Semiconductors sector, including public references (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and private peers such as Cerebras, SambaNova Systems, and Tenstorrent.\n\nThe stage-progression method is the applicable triangulation approach here. Using total capital raised ($52M) as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage advancement yields $129M. A peer-median approach was not viable due to insufficient comparables at the same stage and valuation tier within the semiconductor sector; while 11 same-sector peers exist, fewer than three qualify under adjacent-stage or similar-tier filters, making sector-wide aggregation unreliable.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $109M to $148M, with a median point of $129M. This range reflects upside and downside sensitivity around the single methodologically sound approach available. Key uncertainties include the appropriate stage-progression multiplier for frontier semiconductor technology (which may differ from sector norms), the relevance of available public and private comparables to AheadComputing's specific technology and market position, and the company's actual pre-money valuation on its most recent round, which would refine this proxy-based estimate.",
