      "narrative": "Critical Loop is a Series A climate & energy company founded by Bala Ramamurthy that has raised $49M to date. The broader Climate & Energy sector includes 9 peer companies (1 public, 8 private), with notable peers including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen.\n\nGiven the nascent and heterogeneous nature of frontier climate tech, only one valuation method proved applicable: stage-progression analysis. Using the $49M raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement to subsequent funding rounds yields an implied valuation of $98M. A peer-median approach could not be reliably applied due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the Climate & Energy universe\u2014while 9 sector peers exist, none met the filtering threshold of three or more tightly comparable datapoints.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $83M to $113M, with a median point of $98M. The range reflects reasonable sensitivity bounds around the stage-progression methodology given single-method reliance. Key uncertainties include the absence of granular comparable company data at Critical Loop's specific stage and the wide dispersion in climate tech business models, capital intensity, and time horizons\u2014factors that limit confidence in conventional multiples-based approaches. A more robust second method would materially strengthen conviction in this range.",
