      "narrative": "Aventra is a Seed-stage defense and security company founded by former US military and intelligence personnel, having raised $3M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 10 private and 2 public defense-tech firms, including peers such as UFORCE ($1.0B Seed valuation), Singularity ($400M Series A), and NODA AI ($125M Series A), alongside public comparables DRSHF and IDEAFORGE.NS.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $3M raised as a value proxy and applying a typical 2.5x Seed-to-next-stage multiplier, implies a valuation of $8M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector comparable companies at Seed or Series A stage yields a median valuation of $400M, with a range spanning $125M to $1.0B. The stage-progression method reflects early-stage fundamentals; the peer-median incorporates market pricing for similar-stage defense-tech assets but acknowledges substantial variance in the comparable set.\n\nTriangulating these methods produces a valuation range of $6M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $204M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty around which comparables best reflect Aventra's risk profile and growth trajectory. Key sensitivities include traction on customer acquisition, product development velocity, and whether the peer set's elevated valuations reflect durable market demand or sector-specific valuation inflation. Given Seed-stage information sparsity, the lower quartile of $6M\u2013$50M may be more defensible absent material revenue or customer commitments.",
