      "narrative": "Impossible Metals is a seed-stage climate and energy company founded by Oliver Gunasekara (30+ years in technology, led ARM mobile growth), Jason Gillham (18 years in subsea robotics; founded 2G Robotics, acquired by Voyis in January 2020), and Renee Grogan (sustainability and extractive resources expertise). The company has raised $15M to date. The Climate & Energy sector encompasses 9 private peers and 1 public comparable (LNZA), though a sufficiently narrow peer set at the same stage and valuation tier does not exist for traditional median-based valuation.\n\nGiven the absence of sufficient stage-matched comparables, stage-progression analysis provides the primary valuation framework. Applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier\u2014typical for seed-to-next-stage progression\u2014to the $15M raised as a value proxy yields $37.5M. Bracketing this central case with conservative and optimistic scenarios (\u00b115% variance) produces a low estimate of $32M and a high estimate of $43M.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $32M to $43M, with a median of $38M. Key uncertainties include the absence of directly comparable seed-stage Climate & Energy companies to validate the 2.5x multiplier assumption, the company's path to differentiation within a crowded sector, and subsurface robotic commercialization timelines. Management's track record in scaling and subsystems integration partially mitigates execution risk but does not resolve fundamental market timing questions.",
