      "narrative": "Andrenam is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company founded by Matej Cernosek and Alex Chu that has raised $10M to date. The valuation assessment draws from a peer universe of 10 comparable companies across the sector\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $10M total raised as a proxy for current value and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement, implies a valuation of $25M. Peer-median methodology examined three same-sector and same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014UFORCE (Seed, $1.0B), Singularity (Series A, $400M), and NODA AI (Series A, $125M)\u2014yielding a median valuation of $400M with a range of $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce substantial divergence, reflecting uncertainty in stage-appropriate multiples versus sector-specific peer benchmarking. The triangulated range spans $21M (low), $212M (median), and $460M (high). The wide dispersion reflects the early stage of the company relative to later-stage, better-capitalized peers in the Defense & Security sector. Key uncertainties include Andrenam's progress on key milestones, product maturity relative to comparables, and whether peer multiples reflect sustainable market conditions or temporal valuation inflation in frontier defense tech.",
