      "narrative": "Radiant, a Series D nuclear energy company founded by Doug Bernauer, has raised $465M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 8 peers: 3 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 5 private peers including Oklo, X-Energy, Nano Nuclear Energy, Fuse Energy, and Zap Energy.\n\nStage-progression methodology is the applicable triangulation approach here. Using Radiant's last post-money valuation of $1.0B as the base and applying a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical of Series D progression, this method implies a valuation of $1.5B. A peer-median approach was not applicable due to insufficient comparable datapoints at the same or adjacent stage with similar valuation tier within the narrow nuclear energy sector\u2014while 4 same-sector peers exist, none met the threshold of 3+ qualifying comparables needed to establish statistical reliability.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $1.3B to $1.7B, with a median point of $1.5B. Key uncertainties include the limited depth of direct-stage comparable data and the nascent, heterogeneous nature of the advanced nuclear subsector, which constrains peer-based validation. The valuation rests primarily on stage-progression assumptions rather than market multiples, leaving sensitivity to both the appropriateness of the 1.5x multiplier and Radiant's positioning relative to its less-comparable peer set.",
