      "narrative": "Kairos Power is a late-stage nuclear energy company that has raised $500M+ from inception. The valuation universe comprises 8 comparable firms across the sector: 3 public entities (Oklo, Nano Nuclear Energy, and an SMR-related issuer) and 5 private peers including X-Energy, TerraPower, Fuse Energy, and others operating in advanced reactor development and deployment.\n\nValuation work relied on a single applicable method: stage-progression analysis. Using total capital raised ($500M) as a proxy base value, a 1.2x step-up multiplier typical of late-stage advancement to subsequent funding rounds yields $600M. This reflects the incremental value creation expected between capital raises at this maturity level. Peer-median triangulation was not feasible\u2014while four same-sector comparables exist, insufficient data points meeting strict stage and valuation-tier filters precluded reliable median derivation without introducing sector-wide noise.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $510M to $690M, with a midpoint of $600M. This narrow band reflects reliance on a single methodology and the inherent uncertainty in a capital-raised proxy. Key limitations include the absence of adequate same-stage nuclear peers for cross-validation and limited visibility into technology differentiation, regulatory pathway clarity, and customer offtake agreements. Stronger conviction would require either identification of directly comparable late-stage nuclear firms or sector-specific revenue/deployment metrics.",
