      "narrative": "Astranis, a Series D-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $350M+, is valued against a peer universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers in the same sector, including Sierra Space, Apex Space, and Varda Space Industries.\n\nTwo valuation methods apply to this analysis. Stage-progression anchors to Astranis's last known post-money valuation of $3.5B, applying a typical 1.5x step-up multiplier for Series D advancement, yielding $5.2B. Peer-median triangulation across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Apex Space ($2.3B, Series D), Varda Space Industries ($1.5B, Series C), and Skyryse ($1.1B, Series C)\u2014produces a median of $1.9B, with a range of $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied; while the Space & Aerospace sector median trades at 23.9x P/S across six public tickers, Astranis's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThese two methods triangulate to a valuation range of $1.6B (low) to $6.0B (high), with a median of $3.6B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty: the peer set exhibits substantial valuation heterogeneity, particularly the $8.0B outlier (Sierra Space), and stage-progression relies on the accuracy of the $3.5B base. Revenue visibility and path to profitability remain critical to narrowing this range.",
