      "narrative": "Viridian Space is a pre-seed stage company in Space & Aerospace founded by Rostislav Spektor and Matthew Feldman, having raised $2M+ to date. The sector comprises 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs, though narrow-stage peer pricing data remains sparse.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method is the sole applicable triangulation approach. Using the $2M total raised as a proxy for pre-seed valuation and applying a standard Pre-Seed to next-stage step-up multiplier of 2.5x yields an implied valuation of $5M. Peer-Median analysis cannot be applied: while 11 same-sector peers exist, no subset of three or more companies meets both stage and valuation-tier filters required for reliable median extraction. Public-Comp Anchoring is also inapplicable; the sector median P/S multiple is 23.9x across six public tickers, but Viridian's revenue is not disclosed, preventing ratio application.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $4M (low) to $6M (high), with a median of $5M. This narrow band reflects reliance on a single method and the absence of disclosed financial metrics. Key uncertainties include the company's current revenue run-rate or ARR, which would permit cross-check via public comparables, and the availability of recent private pre-seed or seed financings in adjacent space segments. Additional diligence on product maturity and capital efficiency would refine conviction in this range.",
