      "narrative": "Observable Space is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $90M to date. The valuation landscape for the sector includes six public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) with a median EV/Sales multiple of 23.9x, alongside eight private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs. However, the private peer set lacks sufficient granular comparability at identical stage and valuation tiers to support robust median-based benchmarking.\n\nGiven data constraints, stage-progression analysis emerges as the applicable method. Using total capital raised as a proxy for current valuation ($90M) and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, this method implies a valuation of $180M. Public-comp anchoring cannot be deployed because Observable Space's revenue is not disclosed\u2014a common limitation in private company analysis. Peer-median triangulation is similarly inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparable data points within the narrow Space & Aerospace filter.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $153M to $207M, with a median point of $180M. This range reflects uncertainty inherent in single-method reliance. Key risks to valuation include execution against competitive dynamics within an increasingly crowded space-tech market, capital efficiency relative to peers, and near-term path to revenue inflection. Additional disclosure of revenue traction would enable cross-validation via public-comp multiple anchoring.",
