      "narrative": "Atom Bodies is a Series A-stage biotech company founded by Tyler Hayes, Doug Satzger, and Eric Monsef, having raised $2M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 3 public Biotech & Health comps (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private-sector peers including Colossal Biosciences, Abridge, and Chai Discovery.\n\nOnly the stage-progression method proved applicable to this analysis. Using total capital raised ($2M) as a baseline proxy and applying a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier for Series A progression yields an implied valuation of $4M. The peer-median approach was not viable due to insufficient narrow-stage comparables within the biotech peer set; while 8 same-sector private companies exist, filtering for stage and valuation tier yielded fewer than the required 3 datapoints. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples (median 5.6x across the three public tickers) could not be applied absent the target's revenue, which private companies typically do not disclose.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $3M (low) to $5M (high), with $4M as the median. This narrow range reflects reliance on a single method and should be weighted accordingly. Key uncertainties include the target's undisclosed revenue run rate, competitive positioning within the biotech landscape, and the adequacy of the $2M total raised as a valuation proxy given potential dilution in prior rounds.",
