      "narrative": "Mammoth Biosciences, a Series D biotech company founded by Jennifer Doudna and cofounders, is valued within a peer set of 8 private and 3 public Biotech & Health companies at similar or adjacent stages. The private comp universe includes four primary peers\u2014Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B, Series C), Abridge ($5.3B, Series E), Chai Discovery ($3.8B, Series C), and New Limit ($3.1B, Series C)\u2014spanning a $3.1B to $10.3B valuation range.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the company's $600M total raised as a base proxy and applying a 1.5x multiplier typical of Series D advancement, implied a $900M valuation. The peer-median method across the four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yielded a $4.5B implied value. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (sector median: 5.6x across 3 biotech tickers) was not executable due to the absence of disclosed revenue for this private company.\n\nTriangulation across the two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $765M (low) to $5.2B (high), with a median of $2.7B. The wide range reflects meaningful stage and performance heterogeneity within the peer set. Key uncertainties include the company's current revenue run rate and clinical/commercial progress relative to the named comparables\u2014both critical to narrowing the peer-derived ceiling of $5.2B.",
