      "narrative": "Mazama operates in Climate & Energy and is a Series A company founded by Sriram Vasantharajan that has raised $30M+. The broader sector includes 9 peers across public and private markets (1 public, 8 private), including companies such as Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumQape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen.\n\nValuation analysis relies on stage-progression methodology, which applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage transitions. Using the $30M total raised as a valuation proxy, this method implies a $60M valuation. A peer-median approach was not applicable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables within the Climate & Energy sector; while nine same-sector peers exist, none met the threshold of three or more datapoints when filtered by stage, timing, or valuation tier, making broad-sector comparison unreliable.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $51M to $69M, with a median of $60M. This range reflects the step-up methodology's implied value with downside and upside adjustments accounting for execution risk and market timing. Key uncertainties include the absence of narrow peer validation and the reliance on a single triangulation method. Stage-progression mechanics, while standard, do not account for company-specific traction, capital efficiency, or sector-specific risk factors that would typically emerge during next-round negotiations.",
