      "narrative": "Rainmaker is a Series A drone and autonomous systems company that has raised $25M to date. The valuation universe for this sector comprises 8 private peers\u2014including Zipline, Joby Aviation, Nuro, Archer Aviation, and Elroy Air\u2014with no public comparables available for direct benchmarking.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method is the sole applicable valuation approach given the constraint. Using total capital raised ($25M) as a proxy for post-money valuation and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for progression from Series A to subsequent rounds yields an implied valuation of $50M. The Peer-Median method was not applied; while 5 same-sector peers exist, filtering for identical stage, adjacent-stage, or similar valuation tier produced fewer than the 3 datapoints required for statistical reliability, and a full-sector median would risk material distortion.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $42M (low) to $57M (high), with a median of $50M. This single-method result carries meaningful uncertainty. The absence of same-stage peer data limits cross-validation, and stage-progression multipliers are sensitive to market conditions and company-specific risk profiles not captured here. Confidence in this range would materially improve with either additional same-stage comparable transactions or narrower peer financials. The analyst should view $50M as a point estimate pending further diligence on burn rate, revenue traction, and competitive positioning.",
