      "narrative": "Arc Boats is a Series B stage transportation company founded by Mitch Lee and Ryan Cook that has raised $100M+. The valuation exercise draws on a comparable universe of 7 private frontier-tech transportation firms\u2014including Rivian, The Boring Company, Einride, The ePlane Company, and DeepDive\u2014though no public market comparables exist in this nascent sector.\n\nStage-progression methodology was the applicable triangulation approach. Using the $100M total capital raised as a base value proxy and applying a typical Series B step-up multiplier of 1.9x yields an implied valuation of $190M. Peer-median analysis was not executable; while the transportation sector contains 3 peers, none met narrow filtering criteria (same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-tier valuation bandwidth), and relying on all-sector medians would introduce unacceptable methodological noise.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $162M (low) to $218M (high), with a median point of $190M. This range reflects \u00b115% sensitivity around the stage-progression result given single-method reliance. Key uncertainties include the absence of same-stage transportation peers suitable for median benchmarking and the degree to which $100M in cumulative raise accurately reflects current enterprise value. Investors should weight this estimate accordingly against operational metrics, unit economics, and capital efficiency data not present in this valuation framework.",
