      "narrative": "Shinkei is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Saif Khawaja and Reed Ginsberg that has raised $30M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 private companies and 1 public comparable in the robotics and manufacturing sector, including Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $30M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage progression, yielding $60M. Peer-median analysis across the three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $1.8B. The wide dispersion reflects stage heterogeneity within the peer set (Walden at Seed versus Bedrock and Dexterity at Series B).\n\nThe triangulated analysis across these two methods supports a valuation range of $51M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $855M. The substantial gap between the stage-progression and peer-median results reflects tension between Shinkei's current funding traction and the maturity of late-stage robotics comparables. Key uncertainties include the precise stage positioning relative to peers, revenue and unit economics relative to the peer cohort, and whether peer valuations reflect sector-wide frothiness or durable fundamentals.",
