      "narrative": "Auterion, a Series B defense and security technology company founded by Lorenz Meier and Kevin Sartori, has raised $130M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 10 peers\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private companies\u2014all operating in the Defense & Security sector at equivalent or proximate stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression approach uses the $130M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $247M. The peer-median method references seven same-sector, same-stage comparables (Dream Security at $3.0B, Harmattan AI at $1.4B, Code Metal at $1.2B, Castelion and Defense Unicorns each at $1.0B, plus two others), establishing a median valuation of $1.0B with a range of $300M to $3.0B. These methodologies produce meaningfully divergent results, reflecting heterogeneity within the defense tech peer set.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $210M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $624M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around Auterion's positioning relative to peers\u2014specifically, whether the company's current traction and market opportunity align with upper-quartile performers like Dream Security or more closely resemble earlier-stage comparable growth profiles. Capital efficiency and customer concentration warrant further investigation.",
