      "narrative": "Aalyria, a Series B space and aerospace company founded by Chris Taylor, has raised $130M+ and carries a last post-money valuation of $1.3B. The valuation analysis triangulates across a universe of 5 public comps (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, and Varda Space Industries.\n\nTwo methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $1.3B base, implying $2.5B. Peer-median anchoring across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies yields $1.8B, with a range spanning $1.1B (Skyryse) to $8.0B (Sierra Space). Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied; while the Space & Aerospace sector trades at a 23.9x median P/S across six public companies, Aalyria's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nTriangulation of the two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $1.5B to $2.8B, with a median of $2.1B. This sits modestly above the current $1.3B post-money, consistent with forward-looking stage progression. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion among private peers\u2014a 7x spread between floor and ceiling\u2014and the absence of revenue data, which precludes benchmarking against public multiples. The analysis does not resolve whether Aalyria commands a premium within the peer set.",
