      "narrative": "Agility Robotics, founded by Jonathan Hurst, Damion Shelton, and Mikhail Jones, is a Series D robotics and manufacturing company that has raised over $400M to date. Valuation analysis is anchored to a comparable set of 9 peers (1 public, 8 private), including same-sector companies at Series C through Series E stages: Divergent ($2.3B, Series E), Exotec ($2.0B, Series D), Hadrian ($1.6B, Series C), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B, Series C).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.5x multiplier to a $5.2B base value derived from total capital raised, yielding $7.8B. Peer-median analysis across the 4-company sample yields $1.8B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $2.3B. The stage-progression method treats raised capital as a proxy for underlying value and projects forward momentum; peer-median anchors to observable transactions in the comparable universe but reflects a discrete set of four transactions.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $1.5B (low) to $9.0B (high), with a median of $4.8B. The wide dispersion reflects material tension between extrapolated fundraising trajectory and realized peer valuations. Key uncertainties include the appropriateness of the 1.5x stage multiplier for this sector and whether the peer set fully captures Agility's product-market positioning relative to later-stage funding rounds.",
