      "narrative": "Re:Build Manufacturing is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Miles Arnone, Jeff Wilke, Anthony Manzo, and Michael Foley, with $545M in total capital raised to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of nine private companies and one public comparable in the robotics and manufacturing sector.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $545M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage progression, yielding $1.1B. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Bedrock Robotics (Series B, $1.8B), Dexterity (Series B, $1.6B), and Walden Robotics (Seed, $1.1B)\u2014generating a median valuation of $1.6B with a range of $1.1B to $1.8B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a valuation range of $926M to $1.9B, with a median of $1.4B. Stage-progression and peer multiples converge broadly in the $1.1B\u2013$1.6B band. Key uncertainties include the relevance of Series B comparables to a Series A target and the reliability of total raised as a valuation proxy absent explicit current round data or revenue metrics.",
