      "narrative": "AMP Robotics is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $180M+ to date. The valuation analysis considers a comp universe spanning 9 private robotics firms and 1 public comparable (ticker 277810.KQ), including peers such as Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, and Locus Robotics at Series B and adjacent stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply to this target. The stage-progression method, anchoring to the $30M total-raised proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implies a $60M valuation. The peer-median method derives from a 3-firm comparable set (Bedrock Robotics at $1.8B Series B, Dexterity at $1.6B Series B, and Walden Robotics at $1.1B Seed), yielding a median valuation of $1.6B with a range spanning $1.1B to $1.8B.\n\nThe two methods produce a wide triangulated range from $51M to $1.9B, with a median of $855M. This divergence reflects material tension between valuation implied by capital raised to date versus late-stage peer multiples. The stage-progression result anchors to documented funding history but may underweight market momentum in early-stage robotics. Conversely, peer-median methodology assumes comparability despite AMP's earlier stage and smaller capital base relative to Series B benchmarks. Key uncertainties include whether AMP's operational performance and unit economics justify Series B-level multiples and the degree of stage-adjustment warranted within this sector's rapid growth environment.",
