      "narrative": "Atom Computing is a Series B semiconductor company founded by Ben Bloom and Jonathan King, having raised $60M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparables universe of 11 peers spanning Chips & Semiconductors: three public companies (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and eight private firms including Positron AI, Cerebras, SambaNova Systems, PsiQuantum, and Etched.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply to this stage. The Stage-Progression method uses the $60M raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, implying $114M. The Peer-Median method evaluates five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014SambaNova Systems ($11.0B, Series A), Etched ($5.0B, Series C), d-Matrix ($2.0B, Series C), Positron AI ($1.0B, Series B), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C)\u2014yielding a median valuation of $2.0B and a range of $529M to $11.0B. The wide peer dispersion reflects variance in stage mix and market positioning within the frontier-chip sector.\n\nTriangulating these methods yields a valuation range of $97M to $2.3B, with a median of $1.1B. The substantial spread reflects material uncertainty around Atom's technical differentiation and path to commercialization relative to peers. The Stage-Progression method alone suggests a floor near $100M; peer-median analysis indicates ceiling risk in the $2B+ range absent clear market traction data.",
