      "narrative": "Saildrone is a Series D-stage defense and security company that has raised $300M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a universe of ten comparables: two public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and eight private peers, including Helsing, Saronic, Chaos Industries, and Onebrief operating in the same sector and stage.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised ($1.8B proxy) and a typical Series D step-up multiplier of 1.5x, implies a valuation of $2.6B. Peer-median analysis across the four same-sector Series D comparables yields a median valuation of $6.9B, with a range spanning $2.1B (Onebrief) to $18.0B (Helsing). The dispersion reflects material variance in scale and maturity within the peer set.\n\nSynthesizing both methods produces a triangulated range of $2.2B (low) to $7.9B (high), with a median estimate of $4.8B. The stage-progression method anchors the downside; peer comparables drive the upside. Key uncertainties center on Saildrone's revenue scale and growth trajectory relative to the peer cohort, which spans nearly an order of magnitude at the high end. The wide peer dispersion\u2014particularly the $18.0B valuation for Helsing\u2014underscores material differentiation in capital efficiency or market positioning across this emerging subsector.",
