      "narrative": "Overland AI is a Series A defense and security company founded by Byron Boots, Greg Okopal, and Stephanie Bonk. The valuation analysis draws on a comparables universe of 10 same-sector peers at equivalent or adjacent stage, comprising 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Shield AI.\n\nTwo valuation methods triangulate the company's worth. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x multiplier to Overland's $40M+ total raised, implying $80M. Peer-median analysis across the 10-company Defense & Security set yields a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range spanning $125M to $3.0B; representative peers include Dream Security ($3.0B Series B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B Series B), and Castelion ($1.0B Series B).\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $68M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median estimate of $540M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty about Overland's revenue trajectory, go-to-market traction, and competitive positioning relative to better-funded peers. Stage-progression anchors conservatively; peer medians suggest substantially higher market clearing prices for Series A companies in this sector. Key variables for resolution include customer concentration, technology differentiation within the defense AI subsector, and path to the next funding round.",
