      "narrative": "Primer AI is a Series D-stage defense and security software company that has raised $237M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 4 private companies at identical stage and sector (Helsing, Saronic, Chaos Industries, Onebrief), supplemented by 2 public defense contractors and additional private comparables including Anduril Industries.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a typical 1.5x step-up multiplier for Series D advancement, implies a valuation of $356M. Peer-median methodology across the same-stage, same-sector cohort yields $6.9B, with a range spanning $2.1B (Onebrief) to $18.0B (Helsing). The peer set dispersion reflects meaningful variation in business maturity, customer concentration, and margin profile within defense AI.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $302M (low) to $7.9B (high), with a median of $3.6B. The wide spread reflects structural uncertainty: stage-progression anchors conservatively near capital deployed, while peer-median captures market pricing for defense AI platforms at this stage. Key uncertainties include Primer's revenue scale relative to peers, customer concentration among U.S. defense agencies, and the durability of current market multiples in the sector. Resolution of these factors will determine positioning within the implied range.",
