      "narrative": "True Anomaly is a Defense & Security stage company currently valued at $2.2B following SPAC announcement. The valuation assessment relies on a peer cohort of 14 same-sector companies at similar valuation tiers, spanning both public equities (2 comps: DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and private institutions (8 comps including Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, Saronic, and Quantum-Systems).\n\nThe peer-median method, the primary applicable triangulation approach given available data, yields $1.8B across the 14-company cohort. The peer set ranges from $1.0B at the low end to $9.2B (Saronic, Series D) at the high end, with notable interim comps including Quantum-Systems at $8.0B, Flock Safety at $7.5B, Chaos Industries at $4.5B, and Skydio at $4.4B. This wide dispersion reflects heterogeneity in business model, revenue scale, and customer concentration within the Defense & Security frontier-tech segment.\n\nThe triangulation analysis supports a valuation range of $1.5B to $2.0B (median $1.8B), positioning True Anomaly's current $2.2B valuation above the peer median by approximately 24%. Key uncertainties include the company's actual revenue run-rate relative to peer comparables, customer diversification profile, and execution risk inherent to pre-revenue or early-revenue defense contractors. The limited sample size of public comps (2) constrains confidence in market-implied multiples.",
