      "narrative": "PILGRIM is a Seed-stage defense and security company that has raised $4.3M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 10 companies across the Defense & Security sector\u20142 public names (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, which uses the $4.3M total raised as a proxy for current value and applies a 2.5x multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement, implies a valuation of $11M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector comparables\u2014UFORCE at $1.0B (Seed), Singularity at $400M (Series A), and NODA AI at $125M (Series A)\u2014yields a median valuation of $400M, with a range spanning $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce materially divergent results, suggesting a triangulated range of $9M to $460M with a median of $205M. The stage-progression method reflects PILGRIM's early funding position, while the peer-median approach anchors to funded comparables in the same sector. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the three peer companies, capital efficiency relative to peers, and whether PILGRIM's technology or market position materially justifies a premium or discount to sector medians. Further data on revenue, customer traction, or technology differentiation would narrow this range substantially.",
