      "narrative": "Insitro, a Series C-stage biotech company founded by Daphne Koller, has raised $1.1B+ to date. Valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 3 public Biotech & Health tickers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers, with 3 directly comparable Series C companies: Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the $1.1B raised as a proxy base value and applies a typical 1.7x Series C step-up multiplier, implying a $1.9B valuation. Peer-median analysis across the 3 same-stage, same-sector comparables yields a median valuation of $3.8B, with a range spanning $3.1B to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures. The peer set shows material dispersion, reflecting varied business models and market positions within early-stage biotech.\n\nThe triangulated range is $1.6B to $4.4B, with a median of $2.8B. Key uncertainties include the wide peer range\u2014driven primarily by Colossal's $10.3B outlier\u2014and the absence of revenue-based valuation cross-checks. Stage-progression suggests a floor near $1.9B; peer median anchors the midpoint near $2.8B. Further conviction would require clarity on Insitro's capital efficiency, IP portfolio depth, and clinical timeline relative to the broader cohort.",
