      "narrative": "Charm Industrial is a Series B climate and energy company founded by Peter Reinhardt and Shaun Meehan that has raised over $100M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 private companies and 1 public comparable (Linamar, ticker LNZA) operating in the same sector and stage bands, including KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, Amogy, Helion, and Redwood Materials.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy baseline of $100M and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implies a valuation of $190M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M) yields a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range of $700M to $3.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce a wide triangulated range: low of $162M, median of $595M, and high of $1.1B. This dispersion reflects material uncertainty in early-stage climate tech valuations, where stage-progression mechanics and peer multiples diverge significantly. The peer-median approach assumes Charm's competitive positioning and capital efficiency align with the cohort; stage-progression assumes typical venture returns progression. Resolution of this range depends on operational metrics, capital efficiency, and market timing relative to comparable exit or follow-on valuations.",
