      "narrative": "PsiQuantum is a private-stage semiconductor company founded by Jeremy O'Brien, Terry Rudolph, Peter Shadbolt, and Mark Thompson. The company currently carries a $7B valuation following $1B in total capital raised. Valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 11 companies\u20143 public (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers in the Chips & Semiconductors sector, including SambaNova Systems, Cerebras, Etched, Tenstorrent, and Rebellions.\n\nThe peer-median method, applied across 6 same-sector comparables at similar valuation tiers, yields an implied valuation of $2.5B. The peer set ranges from $2.0B (Tenstorrent, Rebellions, Ouster) to $11.0B (SambaNova Systems), with a median of $2.5B. This single methodological anchor represents the primary triangulation input given data constraints.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $2.1B to $2.9B (median $2.5B), implying a gap of approximately 2.8x between the current stated valuation and peer-derived value. Key uncertainties include: limited methodological diversity (one applicable method); stage and financing dispersion across the peer set; and material variance within comparable valuations. The analysis does not reconcile the current $7B valuation with peer market signals and warrants deeper investigation into company-specific value drivers, IP differentiation, and market timing assumptions not present in comparable data.",
