      "narrative": "d-Matrix is a Series C semiconductor company that has raised $450M to date against a current post-money valuation of $2.0B. The relevant peer universe comprises 11 private and 3 public companies in the chips and semiconductors sector, including adjacent-stage comparables such as Etched ($5.0B, Series C), Tenstorrent ($2.7B, Series D), Positron AI ($1.0B, Series B), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C).\n\nTwo valuation methods triangulate the company's forward value. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier to the $2.0B last post-money, implying $3.4B. Peer-median analysis across the four same-sector/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.9B, with a range spanning $529M to $5.0B. These methods produce meaningfully different signals, reflecting volatility in the frontier-chip subsector and wide dispersion among early-stage semiconductor valuations.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $1.6B (low) to $3.9B (high), with a median of $2.6B. This midpoint stands 30% above the current $2.0B post-money but below the stage-progression upside. Key uncertainties include the timing and magnitude of product commercialization, competitive intensity in custom silicon, and whether the peer set adequately reflects d-Matrix's specific positioning within that spectrum.",
