      "narrative": "Isar Aerospace, a Series C-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $650M+, is valued herein against a comp universe of 5 public peers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private-stage companies in the same sector, including Sierra Space, Varda Space Industries, and Skyryse.\n\nTwo triangulation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $650M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C advancement, implies $1.1B. Peer-median analysis across three same-stage, same-sector comparables\u2014Sierra Space ($8.0B), Varda Space Industries ($1.5B), and Skyryse ($1.1B)\u2014yields a median of $1.5B, with a range of $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 23.9x across the 6-ticker space sector) was not applicable due to the absence of disclosed revenue for the target.\n\nThe triangulated range is $939M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $1.3B. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion in peer valuations\u2014particularly Sierra Space's $8.0B outlier\u2014and the lack of target revenue, which prevents revenue-multiple validation. The analysis suggests a fair value near the $1.3B median, though execution risk and the proprietary nature of launch-vehicle development warrant careful assessment of cash burn and technical milestones.",
