      "narrative": "Exotec, a Series D robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $335M+, is valued at $2.0B post-money. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable set spanning one public company (277810.KQ) and eight private peers, including Divergent ($2.3B, Series E), Hadrian ($1.6B, Series C), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B, Series C).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical for Series D advancement, yielding $3.0B. Peer-median methodology across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables produces $1.6B, reflecting the distribution of Robotics & Manufacturing valuations from $1.0B to $2.3B. The peer cohort's median valuation stands at $1.6B.\n\nThe combined analysis supports a valuation range of $1.4B to $3.4B, with a midpoint of $2.3B. The current $2.0B valuation sits within this range but notably below the stage-progression upside. Key uncertainties include calibration of the 1.5x multiplier to Exotec's specific growth trajectory and the representativeness of the three-company peer set\u2014the broader private peer universe (Divergent, Locus Robotics, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity) exhibits significant dispersion. The $700M gap between peer-median and stage-progression implied values reflects material ambiguity regarding appropriate discount or premium relative to stage peers.",
