      "narrative": "IQM Quantum Computers is a pre-IPO frontier-tech company in quantum computing that has raised \u20ac600M+ to date. The quantum computing sector comprises a sparse comp universe: 3 public peers (IONQ, RGTI, QBTS) and 6 private peers including Quantinuum, IonQ, D-Wave Quantum, Rigetti Computing, and Infleqtion. Given the nascency and heterogeneity of the sector, traditional valuation anchors are constrained.\n\nPeer-median multiples analysis is not applicable here. The quantum computing sector contains only 5 same-sector peers total, and filtering by stage (pre-IPO), recency of funding, or valuation tier yields fewer than three datapoints in any single narrow cohort\u2014the minimum threshold for meaningful median-based triangulation. Applying all-sector median multiples would introduce substantial noise given the wide variance in quantum approach, qubit count, commercialization stage, and revenue (or lack thereof) across peers.\n\nThe absence of a sufficiently dense peer set and the lack of revenue or earnings multiples for most private comparables limits quantitative triangulation. A defensible valuation range cannot be derived from the data provided without accepting high methodological risk. Any range would rest primarily on: (1) funding round pricing precedent and dilution implied by \u20ac600M+ raised; (2) qualitative positioning relative to named peers; and (3) sector-level adoption and capital deployment trends. The key uncertainty remains comparability: each quantum platform targets different qubit modalities, error rates, and use cases, making direct valuation analogy unreliable.",
