      "narrative": "Skyroot Aerospace is a Series C-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $160M to date. Valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private companies in the same sector, with particular focus on 3 same-stage peers: Sierra Space, Varda Space Industries, and Skyryse.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy base value, applies a typical Series C step-up multiplier of 1.7x to $160M, implying $272M. Peer-median analysis across the 3 same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.5B, with a range from $1.1B (Skyryse) to $8.0B (Sierra Space). Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue figures, which private companies typically do not disclose.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $231M to $1.7B, with a median of $886M. The wide spread reflects material dispersion within the peer set\u2014notably, Sierra Space's $8.0B valuation represents an outlier likely attributable to differential stage advancement or capital efficiency. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, launch cadence, and whether Skyroot's capabilities more closely align with mid-tier peers like Varda ($1.5B) or lower-valuation comparables. Without revenue disclosure, sensitivity to near-term commercialization milestones remains high.",
