      "narrative": "Pixxel is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $95M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of five public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and eight private peers in the same sector and stage cohort, including Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Varda Space Industries, Aalyria, and Skyryse.\n\nTwo triangulation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $95M total raised proxy, implying a valuation of $180.5M. Peer-median valuation across the five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median of $1.5B, with a range spanning $1.15B (Skyryse) to $8.0B (Sierra Space). Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $153M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $840M across the two applicable methods. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around stage-appropriate scaling and the heterogeneity of peer valuations within the aerospace sector. Stage-progression yields a more conservative estimate anchored to capital deployed, while peer-median is pulled upward by higher-stage comparables. Resolution depends on near-term revenue trajectory and capital efficiency relative to the peer set.",
