      "narrative": "Monumental is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by Salar al Khafaji and Sebastiaan Visser that has raised $32M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 9 private peers and 1 public comparable in the robotics sector, including Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Hadrian, and Nimble Robotics at similar or adjacent funding stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $32M total raised as a valuation proxy, applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B to next-stage progression, implying a valuation of $61M. Peer-median analysis derives implied valuation from four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with a median valuation of $1.6B (range: $1.0B to $1.8B), directly using this median as the peer-based implication.\n\nThe two methods produce substantially divergent results, yielding a triangulated range of $52M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $843M. The stage-progression method substantially underweights the company relative to sector peers, suggesting either that Monumental commands a material discount to market multiples or that the stage-progression proxy is misaligned with peer valuations. The peer-median method dominates the range width. Key uncertainties include Monumental's technology differentiation relative to the peer set, revenue traction versus comparables, and the appropriate discount or premium to median sector valuation given current funding stage.",
