      "narrative": "Deep Isolation, a Series A nuclear energy company founded by Elizabeth Muller and Richard A. Muller, has raised $26M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a nuclear energy sector universe comprising 3 public comparables (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private peers including Fuse Energy, Oklo, X-Energy, Nano Nuclear Energy, and General Matter.\n\nStage-progression methodology applies directly to Deep Isolation's profile. Using total capital raised of $26M as a valuation proxy and applying a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier for advancement from Series A to the subsequent funding round yields $52M. This represents the primary quantitative anchor given the company's stage and capital history.\n\nPeer-median triangulation is not applicable. While 4 nuclear energy peers exist in the broader dataset, insufficient datapoints meet narrow filtering criteria (same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar valuation tier)\u2014fewer than the minimum 3 required for robust median calibration. Reliance on an all-sector median would introduce unacceptable methodological noise.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $44M to $60M, with a median of $52M supported by the stage-progression method. Key uncertainties include the absence of narrow-peer transaction data, which limits sensitivity analysis, and the nascent nature of the nuclear energy sector itself, where comparable growth and exit multiples remain sparse. This range reflects capital efficiency assumptions typical of Series A progression rather than operational or market-traction metrics.",
