      "narrative": "Delian Alliance Industries is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company that has raised $14M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of 3 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014UFORCE (Seed, $1.0B), Singularity (Series A, $400M), and NODA AI (Series A, $125M)\u2014alongside broader market context of 10 public and private defense-tech peers including Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Shield AI.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement to the $14M capital base, implying $35M. Peer-median methodology anchors to the three comparables' median valuation of $400M, with a range spanning $125M to $1.0B. The peer-median approach carries material weight given the tightness of the Defense & Security frontier-tech cohort and direct stage/sector alignment.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $30M to $460M, with a median of $218M. The wide dispersion reflects genuine uncertainty around Delian's relative competitive positioning, technology differentiation, and capital efficiency versus named peers. The stage-progression method suggests a floor near $30M; peer comparables suggest a broad ceiling near $400\u2013460M depending on assumed competitive tier. Key sensitivities include clarity on product-market fit, customer traction relative to UFORCE and Singularity, and defensibility of any technical moat in a crowded defense-innovation landscape.",
