      "narrative": "Starpath Robotics is a Series A-stage space & aerospace company founded by Saurav Shroff, Mihir Gondhalekar, and Jason Zang that has raised $14.5M+ to date. The sector comprises 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs, though direct same-stage peer valuations remain sparse.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the primary applicable method given data constraints. Using total capital raised ($14.5M+) as a proxy baseline of $50M and applying a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier for Series A-to-next-stage advancement yields an implied valuation of $100M. Peer-median triangulation was not feasible; while 11 same-sector peers exist, fewer than 3 occupy identical stage or valuation tiers, and applying an all-sector median would introduce undue noise. Public-comp anchoring via the Space & Aerospace P/S median of 23.9x across the 5 public tickers could not be executed absent the target's revenue figures, which private companies typically withhold.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $85M\u2013$115M, with a median point of $100M. This range rests entirely on stage-progression methodology and therefore carries material uncertainty around the appropriateness of the 2.0x multiplier for this specific market, company maturity, and capital efficiency. Revenue disclosure and expanded peer financials would materially tighten confidence bounds.",
