      "narrative": "Locus Robotics, a Series F robotics and manufacturing company, is valued at $2.0B post-money following $438M in total capital raised. The valuation analysis benchmarks against a comp universe of nine peers: eight private robotics firms (including Divergent at $2.3B, Exotec at $2.0B, and Bedrock Robotics at $1.8B) and one public comparable.\n\nTwo methods were applied to triangulate fair value. Stage-progression analysis, anchoring to the $2.0B last post-money valuation and applying a typical Series F-to-next-stage step-up multiplier of 1.3x, implies $2.6B. Peer-median analysis across seven same-sector, similar-valuation-tier robotics companies yields a median of $1.6B, with a range of $1.0B to $2.3B. The peer set reflects a mix of later-stage (Divergent at Series E, Exotec at Series D) and earlier-stage (Bedrock at Series B, Dexterity at Series B) companies, suggesting reasonable cross-stage comparability.\n\nTriangulation of both methods produces a valuation range of $1.4B (low) to $3.0B (high), with a median of $2.1B. The current $2.0B valuation sits near the lower bound of this range. Key uncertainties include relative revenue multiples and margin profiles across the peer set, as well as the representativeness of Stage F progression multiples in a market where funding dynamics remain volatile.",
