      "narrative": "D-Wave Quantum operates in the quantum computing sector as a publicly traded company. The peer universe consists of three publicly listed quantum computing firms: IonQ, Rigetti Computing, and Infleqtion, alongside seven private-stage competitors including Quantinuum and Xanadu Quantum Technologies.\n\nThe peer-median method provides the primary valuation anchor. Across the three same-sector, same-stage public comparables, the median valuation stands at $4.5B, with a range spanning $1.9B (Infleqtion) to $13.0B (IonQ). This dispersion reflects material differences in technology approach, commercial traction, or investor sentiment within the nascent quantum computing market. D-Wave's current public valuation of $6.27B sits above the peer median, suggesting market participants are pricing the company at a premium to the comparable set midpoint.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range, informed by peer analysis, suggests a defensible midpoint of $4.5B with a low-to-high band of $3.8B to $5.2B. D-Wave's actual $6.27B valuation exceeds this range by approximately 40% relative to the median. Key uncertainties limiting precision include the early-stage, heterogeneous nature of quantum computing technology platforms\u2014making direct revenue or customer multiples unreliable\u2014and the limited sample size of public comparables. Additional methodologies (revenue multiples, discounted cash flow) are not applicable given the sector's development stage and capital-intensity.",
