      "narrative": "Skyryse, a Series C-stage aerospace company founded by Mark Groden, is valued at $1.15B post-money following $500M+ in total capital raised. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 5 public Space & Aerospace equities (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including Sierra Space, Varda Space Industries, and Impulse Space.\n\nTwo primary valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier to the $1.1B last post-money valuation, implying $2.0B. Peer-median triangulation across 5 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a $2.0B implied value, with the peer set ranging from $1.3B (Aalyria, Series B) to $8.0B (Sierra Space, Series C). Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied, as Skyryse's revenue is not disclosed. The target's relatively modest positioning within the peer range\u2014particularly versus the outlier Sierra Space valuation of $8.0B\u2014suggests meaningful dispersion in how the market prices early-stage aerospace operators.\n\nThe two-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $1.7B\u2013$2.3B, with a median of $2.0B. This implies 74% upside from current post-money. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, the sustainability of near-term aerospace funding multiples, and Skyryse's differentiated position within an increasingly crowded frontier-tech sector.",
