      "narrative": "Poseidon Aerospace is a seed-stage space and aerospace company founded by David Zagaynov, Parker Tenney, and Isaac Baumstark. The company has raised $12M+ to date. The valuation universe includes 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers, though narrow-stage filtering within Space & Aerospace yielded insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage peers for reliable median benchmarking.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the primary applicable method. Using total capital raised of $12M as a valuation proxy and applying a typical 2.5x seed-to-next-stage step-up multiplier yields an implied valuation of $30M. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples cannot be applied without disclosed revenue; the sector median P/S is 23.9x across six public tickers, but remains inapplicable to a private target lacking revenue disclosure. Peer-median analysis similarly lacks sufficient datapoints within tight stage and tier filters.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $26M to $34M, with $30M as the midpoint. This range reflects low confidence driven by reliance on a single applicable method and the absence of revenue-based cross-checks or narrow private comparables at seed stage. Key uncertainties include the company's actual revenue run rate, capital efficiency relative to public peers, and typical step-up multiples in the current seed-to-series-A market for aerospace ventures. Additional diligence on unit economics and addressable market would strengthen conviction.",
