      "narrative": "CarbonCapture Inc., a Series B climate technology company founded by Adrian Corless, is evaluated against a comparable universe of 9 private and 1 public company in the Climate & Energy sector, including peers such as KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the company's $80M total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B-to-next-stage step-ups, yielding $152M. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: KoBold Metals at $3.0B (Series C), Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B (Series C), and Amogy at $700M (Series C). The median valuation across these three peers is $1.0B, with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B.\n\nThe two methods triangulate to a valuation range of $129M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $576M. This wide spread reflects material uncertainty inherent in peer-comparable analysis given the nascent stage of the climate technology sector and substantial variance in peer valuations. The stage-progression method suggests more conservative positioning relative to the peer set. Key uncertainties include the relevance of Series C comparables to a Series B-stage target and the heterogeneity of capital intensity and development timelines across climate technology subsectors.",
