      "narrative": "OpenStar is a seed-stage climate and energy company founded by Ratu Mataira and Thomas Berry, having raised $35M to date. The valuation framework draws on a comp universe of 9 same-sector peers: 1 public company (LNZA) and 8 private firms including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen.\n\nThe analysis employs stage-progression methodology, which is applicable given the seed stage context. Using a $10.0B total-raised proxy as the base value and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical for seed-to-next-stage progression, this method implies a valuation of $25.0B. A peer-median approach was not viable; while 9 climate and energy peers exist, filtering for same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier companies yielded fewer than the required three datapoints, making sector-wide median comparison insufficiently precise.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $21.2B (low) to $28.7B (high), with a median of $25.0B. This single-method range reflects meaningful uncertainty: the analysis is anchored to one methodology, and the absence of tightly comparable seed-stage peers in climate tech limits cross-validation. Key unknowns include OpenStar's specific technology focus, burn rate relative to the $35M raised, and path to next funding round. Given reliance on stage-progression alone, investors should treat this as a directional estimate pending additional peer data or clearer comparable transactions.",
