      "narrative": "Archer Materials is a public-stage quantum computing company currently valued at A$59.9M (~US$39M) following $25M+ in total capital raised. The quantum computing sector peer universe comprises 10 comparable companies across public and private stages, including three public peers (IonQ, Rigetti Computing, D-Wave Quantum via ticker QBTS) and seven private counterparts such as Quantinuum and Infleqtion.\n\nValuation analysis relies on peer-median methodology applied to four same-sector, same-stage public comparables. The median valuation across IonQ ($13.0B), D-Wave Quantum ($6.3B), Rigetti Computing ($4.5B), and Infleqtion ($1.9B) is $5.4B. This peer range spans $1.9B to $13.0B, reflecting material dispersion within the public quantum computing cohort. The peer-median approach yields an implied valuation of $5.4B for Archer Materials.\n\nTriangulation analysis supports a valuation range of $4.6B (low) to $6.2B (high), with a median of $5.4B. This implies a potential upside multiple of 118x to 159x relative to Archer's current market valuation. Key uncertainties include the maturity variance among public comparables\u2014IonQ and D-Wave command substantially higher valuations than Rigetti and Infleqtion\u2014and the absence of additional valuation methodologies (DCF, revenue multiples) in the available data. Archer's path to realizing peer-comparable valuations depends on technical progress and commercial execution relative to the incumbent cohort.",
