      "narrative": "RISE Robotics is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Arron Acosta and Blake Sessions that has raised $22M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private firms and 1 public company across the robotics sector, including peers at seed through Series B stages such as Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B seed).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression methodology, using the $22M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implies a valuation of $44M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $1.8B. This wide dispersion reflects meaningful stage and maturity differences within the peer set.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $37M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $847M. The substantial gap between stage-progression and peer-median methods reflects RISE's earlier stage relative to Series B peers and the heterogeneity of robotics valuations. Key uncertainties include unit economics, capital efficiency relative to peers, and whether the company tracks closer to early-stage or late-stage comparable trajectories. Revenue traction and path to profitability will be critical to narrowing this range.",
