      "narrative": "Path Robotics, a Series D robotics and manufacturing company founded by Andy and Alex Lonsberry, has raised $271M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private robotics firms and 1 public company, with primary focus on four same-sector peers at adjacent stages: Divergent (Series E, $2.3B), Exotec (Series D, $2.0B), Hadrian (Series C, $1.6B), and Nimble Robotics (Series C, $1.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $271M total raised as a proxy base and applies a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical for Series D advancement, yielding $406M. Peer-median analysis anchors to the four comparable companies, which span valuations of $1.0B to $2.3B with a median of $1.8B. This reflects Path's positioning relative to same-stage and near-stage robotics peers.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $346M (low), $1.1B (median), and $2.1B (high). The stage-progression method supports the lower bound, while peer comparability\u2014particularly Exotec's $2.0B Series D valuation\u2014supports the upper range. Key uncertainties include Path's current revenue run rate, unit economics relative to peers, and whether recent market dynamics have compressed or expanded robotics sector multiples since the peer valuations were established.",
