      "narrative": "Vertical Semiconductor is a Seed-stage chip design company founded by Joshua Perozek, Cynthia Liao, and Tomas Palacios. The valuation assessment draws on a comp universe of 11 private and public peers in the Chips & Semiconductors sector, including public comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and private peers such as Cerebras, SambaNova Systems, and Etched.\n\nA peer-median approach proved inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables within the narrow peer set\u2014the Chips & Semiconductors universe yielded only one adjacent-stage datapoint, below the threshold of three required for reliable triangulation. Consequently, valuation relies on stage-progression methodology, which applies a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to the subsequent financing round. Using the company's $11M total raised as a proxy for current value, this method implies a valuation of $28M.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $23M to $32M, centered on $28M. Key uncertainties include the absence of direct peer benchmarks at equivalent stage and valuation tier, which limits calibration against market comparables. Additionally, the applicability of a 2.5x multiplier depends on execution velocity and market conditions specific to frontier semiconductor ventures, neither of which can be assessed from valuation data alone.",
