      "narrative": "Amogy, a Series C climate and energy technology company founded by Seonghoon Woo, is valued at $700M post-money following $300M+ in total funding. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable set spanning one public company (LNZA) and eight private firms in the climate and energy sector at similar or adjacent stages, including KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, Helion, Redwood Materials, and QuantumScape.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using a 1.7x multiplier typical for Series C to next-stage advancement, implies a valuation of $1.2B from the $700M base. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector comparables\u2014Redwood Materials at $6.0B (Series D), KoBold Metals at $3.0B (Series C), and Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B (Series C)\u2014yields a median of $3.0B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $6.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $1.0B (low) to $3.4B (high), with a median of $2.1B. The current $700M valuation sits below both methods, suggesting potential upside on Series D or later funding rounds. Key uncertainties include the timing and terms of the next funding event, relative competitive positioning within the narrowing Climate & Energy VC window, and technology commercialization progress. The wide peer range ($1.0B\u2013$6.0B) reflects heterogeneous company maturities and capital intensity across the sector.",
