      "narrative": "Augury is a Series F robotics and manufacturing diagnostics company that has raised $369M to date. The valuation landscape for this sector comprises one public comparable (277810.KQ) and eight private peers including Locus Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, Bedrock Robotics, and Dexterity, though none operate at a sufficiently tight peer set (same stage, adjacent stage, and similar valuation tier simultaneously) to support reliable median peer multiples.\n\nGiven data constraints, the stage-progression method is the primary applicable triangulation approach. Using total capital raised as a value proxy and applying a 1.3x step-up multiplier typical for Series F advancement yields an implied valuation of $480M. This method rests on the assumption that the 1.3x multiplier reflects realistic market conditions for this stage and sector.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $408M (low) to $552M (median to high), centered on $480M. Key uncertainties include the absence of a robust peer median\u2014the broader robotics sector contains sufficient comparables, but filtering for stage, tier, and operational similarity reduces sample size below three datapoints\u2014and reliance on a single methodological input. Revenue trajectory, unit economics, and customer concentration would materially refine this range but are not available in current data.",
