      "narrative": "Cache Energy is a Seed-stage climate and energy company founded by Arpit Dwivedi that has raised $8.5M to date. The broader Climate & Energy sector includes 9 private peers and 1 public comparable (LNZA), though a sufficiently tight peer set at the same stage and valuation tier does not exist to support median-based valuation.\n\nGiven the nascent peer universe at Seed stage within this sector, the Stage-Progression method is the applicable triangulation approach. This method applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier to the $8M raised proxy, reflecting typical progression economics from Seed to subsequent financing rounds. This yields an implied valuation of $21M. A sensitivity band around this point estimate\u2014accounting for variance in step-up magnitude and earlier-stage risk\u2014supports a range of $18M (low) to $24M (high).\n\nThe analysis supports a median valuation of $21M with a reasonable range of $18M\u2013$24M. The primary uncertainty is the absence of narrow-stage peer data; the stage-progression method relies on historical step-up multiples rather than direct comparable transaction evidence. A fuller peer set\u2014either through additional Seed-stage closings in climate tech or adjacent subsector data\u2014would strengthen conviction in this range. Current raised capital and founder pedigree provide the floor; execution risk and market timing for the next round represent the key downside and upside vectors.",
