      "narrative": "Velaura AI is a Series C-stage semiconductor company founded by Rajiv Khemani, Barun Kar, Saptadeep Pal, and Patrick Xu. The valuation analysis triangulates across a comp universe of 3 public peers (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private frontier-tech companies in the Chips & Semiconductors sector, including same-stage comparables Etched ($5.0B), d-Matrix ($2.0B), and DEEPX ($529M).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses the company's $343M in total raised capital as a proxy baseline, applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C progression, yielding $583M. The peer-median method isolates three same-sector, same-stage comparables with a median valuation of $2.0B and a range of $529M to $5.0B. This reflects wide dispersion in the AI-chip segment, where valuations depend materially on perceived differentiation and deployment traction.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a valuation range of $496M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.3B. The stage-progression floor and peer-median midpoint anchor the lower and central estimates. Key uncertainties include whether Velaura's technical roadmap and go-to-market execution align with higher-valued peers like Etched, or whether market conditions warrant positioning closer to DEEPX. Additional clarity on capital deployment efficiency and customer adoption will be necessary to narrow the range.",
