      "narrative": "Rugged Robotics is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Derrick J. Morse and Logan Farrell, having raised $12M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 9 private peers and 1 public company in the robotics sector, including adjacent-stage companies such as Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses the $12M raised as a proxy for current value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $24M. The peer-median method examines three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables, arriving at a median valuation of $1.6B with a range of $1.1B to $1.8B. These peers span Series B and Seed stages, introducing stage-related variance.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a range of $20.4M to $1.9B, with a median of $837M. The wide dispersion reflects material tension between stage-based progression ($24M) and peer-based valuation ($1.6B), suggesting significant uncertainty around whether Rugged Robotics' operational metrics and market position align with the peer set. Resolution of this gap requires clarity on revenue, growth rate, and competitive positioning relative to the three comparable firms.",
