      "narrative": "Chemify, a Series B biotech company founded by Leroy Cronin, has raised $93M to date. Valuation analysis draws on a comparables universe of 3 public peers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private companies across the Biotech & Health sector, with particular weight given to 4 same-stage or adjacent-stage private peers: Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B, Series C), Chai Discovery ($3.8B, Series C), New Limit ($3.1B, Series C), and Eikon Therapeutics ($539M, Series B).\n\nTwo valuation methods apply. Stage-progression, using the $93M raised as a proxy for current value and applying a 1.9x multiplier typical for Series B advancement, implies $177M. The peer-median method anchors on the four comparable companies, which span $539M to $10.3B with a median of $3.5B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures.\n\nTriangulating these two methods yields a valuation range of $150M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.8B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty in stage-comparable maturity and capital intensity within the biotech sector. Eikon Therapeutics at $539M and the Series C cohort at $3.1B\u2013$10.3B bracket the implied range. Key uncertainties include the competitive positioning of Chemify's core technology, clinical or commercial traction not visible in capital raised, and typical valuation expansion dynamics at the Series B-to-C inflection.",
