      "narrative": "Unspun, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Beth Esponnette, Walden Lam, and Kevin Martin, has raised $57M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 peers\u20141 public and 8 private\u2014including Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, and Walden Robotics, spanning the same sector and adjacent stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression valuation, using the $57M raised as a proxy for post-money value, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $114M. Peer-median valuation references three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with a median valuation of $1.6B (range: $1.1B\u2013$1.8B). This method reflects the positioning of later-stage peers such as Bedrock Robotics at $1.8B and Dexterity at $1.6B.\n\nThe triangulated range spans $97M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $882M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty in stage mapping and peer applicability. The stage-progression method anchors conservatively near recent capital; peer multiples suggest substantially higher valuations typical of maturing robotics ventures. Key uncertainties include the degree to which Series B comparables apply to an early Series A, revenue traction not reflected in the data, and the timing between this analysis and the company's next funding event.",
