      "narrative": "Sabanto is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Craig Rupp that has raised $20M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 9 comparable companies\u20141 public and 8 private\u2014including Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, and Locus Robotics.\n\nTwo methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $20M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to later-stage advancement, yielding $40M. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector comparables at Series B and Seed stages (Bedrock Robotics at $1.8B, Dexterity at $1.6B, and Walden Robotics at $1.1B), producing a median valuation of $1.6B with a range spanning $1.1B to $1.8B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods produces a range of $34M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $845M. The wide dispersion reflects material tension between early-stage funding volume and peer comparables at more advanced stages. Key uncertainties include the applicability of later-stage peer valuations to an earlier-stage company and whether the stage-progression method appropriately captures the sector's capital intensity and growth trajectory. Additional visibility on Sabanto's revenue, unit economics, and technology differentiation would narrow the range materially.",
