      "narrative": "Mythic is a Series D semiconductor design company founded by Mike Henry and Dave Fick that has raised $125M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 11 peers\u20143 public companies (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private frontier-chip firms including Tenstorrent, Cerebras, and SambaNova Systems.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, anchoring to the $125M total raised as a proxy baseline, applies a typical Series D step-up multiplier of 1.5x, yielding $188M. Peer-median analysis examines four same-sector and stage-adjacent comparables: Etched ($5.0B, Series C), Tenstorrent ($2.7B, Series D), d-Matrix ($2.0B, Series C), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C). The median valuation across this set is $2.4B, with a range spanning $529M to $5.0B.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $159M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median of $1.3B. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty in how to weight stage-progression mechanics against peer multiples in an early-stage, capital-intensive sector where outcomes remain unproven. Stage-progression alone suggests modest valuation; peer medians imply substantially higher multiples. Key uncertainties include competitive position relative to named peers, pathway to revenue, and the sustainability of current financing multiples in the frontier-chip space.",
