      "narrative": "Xsight Labs is a Series D semiconductor company that has raised $281M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a peer universe of 11 comparable companies spanning the chips and semiconductors sector\u2014three public (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and eight private firms including Tenstorrent, Cerebras, and Etched at similar or adjacent stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a baseline proxy and applying a typical Series D step-up multiplier of 1.5x, implies a valuation of $422M. Peer-median analysis across four direct comparables (Tenstorrent at $2.7B Series D, Etched at $5.0B Series C, d-Matrix at $2.0B Series C, and DEEPX at $529M Series C) yields a median valuation of $2.4B, with a range spanning $529M to $5.0B. The dispersion reflects stage and market-timing variation among the peer set.\n\nThe two methods produce materially different results, anchoring a triangulated range of $358M (conservative, stage-progression-weighted floor) to $2.7B (peer-median-anchored ceiling), with a midpoint of $1.4B. Key uncertainties driving this wide band include the relative maturity and revenue profile of Xsight Labs versus peers, and the timing and terms of comparable funding rounds. Resolution of commercial traction metrics and capital efficiency relative to the peer cohort would narrow this range substantially.",
