      "narrative": "Evozyne is a Series B\u2013stage biotech company founded by Andrew Ferguson, Rama Ranganathan, and Jeff Aronin, having raised $144M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 8 private companies and 3 public biotech comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) in the Biotech & Health sector.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $144M capital raised proxy, implying a valuation of $274M. Peer-median analysis across four same-stage or adjacent-stage biotechs yields a median valuation of $3.5B, with a range spanning $539M (Eikon Therapeutics, Series B) to $10.3B (Colossal Biosciences, Series C). Public-comp anchoring using a sector P/S median of 5.6x cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures. The wide spread between peer valuations reflects material heterogeneity in stage maturity and commercial progress within the comparable set.\n\nTriangulation across both applicable methods supports a valuation range of $233M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.9B. The substantial gap between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects tension between capital-efficiency metrics and peer trading multiples. Key uncertainties include clinical development status, IP defensibility, and revenue trajectory relative to the Series C cohort peers.",
