      "narrative": "Orbit Fab is a Series A space and aerospace company founded by Daniel Faber and Jeremy Schiel that has raised $28.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 5 public-market Space & Aerospace peers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private companies including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nGiven data limitations, stage-progression methodology is the primary applicable approach. Using total capital raised ($28.5M) as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A progression to subsequent stages yields an implied valuation of $57M. Peer-median analysis is not applicable: while 11 same-sector peers exist in the broader dataset, narrowing to same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables with similar valuation tiers yields fewer than the three datapoints necessary for robust benchmarking. Public-comp anchoring via the sector's 23.9x median price-to-sales multiple cannot be applied due to absence of disclosed revenue figures for the private target.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $48M to $66M, centered on $57M. This narrow range reflects reliance on a single method and underscores key uncertainties: the absence of revenue or comparable private transaction multiples in the space and aerospace sector limits precision. Investors should treat this as a preliminary orientation pending disclosure of financial metrics or identification of tighter private peer benchmarks.",
