      "narrative": "Ultima Genomics is a Series C-stage biotech company that has raised $700M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private-stage biotech firms operating in genomics and related health technology, with particular relevance assigned to same-stage peers Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. The stage-progression method applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $700M capital proxy, yielding $1.2B. The peer-median approach references the three same-sector, same-stage comparables, with a median valuation of $3.8B and a range spanning $3.1B to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied due to absence of disclosed revenue figures, which is standard for private companies.\n\nSynthesizing these two methods produces a triangulated range of $1.0B (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median of $2.5B. The wide dispersion between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects the heterogeneity within the Series C biotech cohort; peer valuations exhibit material variance ($3.1B\u2013$10.3B spread), suggesting stage advancement alone underweights Ultima's apparent competitive position. Key uncertainties include revenue scale, unit economics, and the specific technology differentiation relative to the peer set.",
