      "narrative": "Helios is a Series A climate and energy company founded by Jonathan Geifman, Elad Geffen, Guy Amir, John Hausner, and Ohad Hallak. The target sector includes 9 private peers and 1 public comparable (LNZA), though none form a sufficiently tight peer set at the same stage and valuation tier for meaningful median analysis.\n\nStage-progression valuation applies here as the primary method. Using total capital raised of $26M as a baseline proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage progression yields $52M. This method is grounded in observed stage-to-stage venture capital markup patterns and is directly applicable given Helios's position pre-Series B.\n\nThe peer-median approach is not applicable. While 9 same-sector peers exist (including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen), none satisfy filters for same-stage, adjacent-stage, and similar-tier valuation simultaneously. A broad sector median would introduce material noise and is therefore excluded.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $44M to $60M, with a median of $52M. This range reflects reliance on a single methodology; key uncertainties include the true applicability of the 2.0x multiplier to Helios's specific market position and stage dynamics, and the absence of narrower peer validation. Additional data on comparable Series A-to-B stage transitions within climate tech would narrow the range materially.",
