      "narrative": "Heart Aerospace, a Series B space and aerospace company founded by Anders and Klara Forslund, has raised $185M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 5 public companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Varda Space Industries, Aalyria, and Skyryse.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $185M total raised as a proxy base value and applying a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of $352M. Peer-median analysis across five same-sector and same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.5B, with a range spanning $1.1B (Skyryse) to $8.0B (Sierra Space). The public-comp anchoring method cannot be applied due to absence of revenue data.\n\nTriangulating the two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $299M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $926M. The wide dispersion reflects meaningful heterogeneity within the peer set: stage-progression suggests a more conservative midpoint consistent with earlier funding rounds, while peer-median anchoring captures the premium multiples commanded by later-stage aerospace entrants. Key uncertainties center on Heart Aerospace's product differentiation, nearness to revenue inflection, and execution relative to the Sierra Space and Cowboy Space Corporation cohort.",
