      "narrative": "Peak Energy, founded by Landon Mossburg and Liam O'Connor, is a Series A climate and energy company that has raised $65M to date. The broader Climate & Energy sector comprises 1 public comparable (LNZA) and 8 private peers including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen, though none provide sufficient overlap on stage and valuation tier for reliable peer-median analysis.\n\nGiven the absence of a cohesive same-stage peer set, valuation relies on stage-progression methodology. Using total capital raised ($65M) as a proxy for post-money valuation and applying a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A-to-subsequent-round progression yields an implied valuation of $130M. This reflects the expected step-up in enterprise value as the company advances financing stages.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $110M to $150M, with $130M as the central point. The range reflects typical variance around stage-progression mechanics rather than cross-sectional peer support. Key uncertainties remain the absence of direct comparable transactions at the same stage and tier, and the inherent sensitivity of the 2.0x multiplier to Peak Energy's specific growth trajectory, capital efficiency, and technology differentiation relative to the broader climate tech landscape.",
