      "narrative": "Aerospacelab, a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac200M+, was valued using peer-median triangulation against five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Varda Space Industries ($1.5B, Series C), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B, Series C).\n\nThe peer-median method yielded an implied valuation of $1.5B, with the five-company set spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples was not applicable; the Space & Aerospace sector median trades at 23.9x sales across six public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL), but Aerospacelab's revenue was not available to apply this cross-check.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $1.3B to $1.7B, centered at $1.5B. This range reflects the tight clustering of same-stage peers (Cowboy Space at $2.0B and Aalyria at $1.3B) while acknowledging variance introduced by Series C outliers in the comp set. Key uncertainties include Aerospacelab's revenue scale relative to peers and its product-market positioning within the heterogeneous space sector. The single-method result limits confidence; revenue disclosure would enable public-market cross-validation.",
