      "narrative": "Nomagic is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $97M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies, supplemented by a broader universe of eight private robotics firms and one public comparable.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply. Stage-progression anchors to the $97M total raised as a proxy for current valuation, applying a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $184M. Peer-median analysis examines four robotics companies\u2014Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), Hadrian ($1.6B, Series C), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B, Series C)\u2014producing a median valuation of $1.6B with a range of $1.0B to $1.8B. The stage-progression method reflects Nomagic's actual capital deployed; the peer-median reflects market pricing of comparable-stage competitors, though peer valuations span a wide range reflecting heterogeneity in unit economics and growth trajectories.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $157M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $905M. Key uncertainties include whether Nomagic's operational metrics and growth rate align with higher-valued peers like Bedrock, or with lower-valued later-stage players like Nimble. The 12x spread between methods reflects the wide dispersion in peer valuations and the limited precision of stage-progression alone.",
