      "narrative": "Nu Quantum is a Series A quantum computing company that has raised $60M to date. The quantum computing sector comprises 11 total comparables: 3 public peers (IonQ, Rigetti Computing, D-Wave Quantum) and 8 private companies including Quantinuum and Infleqtion.\n\nThe analysis applies one valuation method. Stage-progression triangulation uses the $60M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical for Series A advancement to the next funding stage, yielding $120M. The peer-median approach is not applicable; while 5 same-sector peers exist in quantum computing, none satisfy the narrow filter criteria of same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier comparables needed for reliable cross-sectional analysis. A sector-wide median would introduce excessive noise given the heterogeneity of business models and development stages across quantum modalities.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $102M (low) to $138M (high), with a median point of $120M. This range reflects a single-method analysis, which materially limits conviction. Key uncertainties include the absence of sufficient near-peer transaction data to validate the 2.0x step-up assumption and the broad dispersion in quantum computing valuations driven by differing technical approaches (superconducting, ion trap, photonic) and commercialization timelines. Additional diligence on comparable Series A-to-B step-ups within quantum or adjacent hardware sectors would strengthen the analysis.",
