      "narrative": "Hadean is a Series B-stage defense and security company founded by Craig Beddis and Aidan Hobson Sayers, having raised $40M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 10 companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers operating in Defense & Security at similar stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method, anchoring to $40M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implies a valuation of $76M. The peer-median method examined 7 same-sector, same-stage comparables including Dream Security ($3.0B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), Castelion ($1.0B), and Defense Unicorns ($1.0B), yielding a median valuation of $1.0B with a range of $300M to $3.0B.\n\nThe two methods diverge significantly, reflecting fundamental uncertainty about Hadean's relative competitive position and market traction within the Defense & Security sector. A triangulated range of $65M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $538M, captures this dispersion. The wide range reflects the material gap between stage-based progression and peer comparables. Key uncertainties center on: differentiation relative to the peer set; revenue traction and margin profile; and customer concentration in defense procurement. The peer-median approach likely applies only if Hadean demonstrates platform characteristics and customer stickiness comparable to the upper quartile of the comp set.",
