      "narrative": "Comand AI is a seed-stage Defense & Security company founded by Lo\u00efc Mougeolle and Antoine Chassan that has raised \u20ac11.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 10 private companies and 2 public entities operating in the same sector. The private peer set includes UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic; public comparables are DRSHF and IDEAFORGE.NS.\n\nThe peer-median method, the applicable triangulation approach, evaluated three same-sector peers at seed and adjacent Series A stages: UFORCE at $1.0B valuation, Singularity at $400M, and NODA AI at $125M. The median of this three-company set is $400M, with a range spanning $125M to $1.0B. This method directly informs the valuation estimate given the limited data granularity at the seed stage and the constrained applicability of revenue or earnings multiples.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $340M (low) to $460M (high), centered on $400M. This range reflects peer positioning but remains sensitive to two primary uncertainties: the degree to which Comand AI's technical differentiation and market traction align with the highest-valued peers in the set, and the broader funding environment's appetite for early-stage defense-tech capital deployment. The single-method foundation limits conviction; additional data on revenue run-rate, customer commitments, or technology benchmarks would strengthen the analysis.",
