      "narrative": "Axelera AI is a Series C-stage semiconductor company founded by Fabrizio Del Maffeo that has raised $450M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 11 peers spanning public equities (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and private companies in the Chips & Semiconductors sector, with particular focus on three same-stage private comparables: Etched ($5.0B), d-Matrix ($2.0B), and DEEPX ($529M).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy for current value, applied a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $765M. Peer-median analysis across the three same-sector, same-stage comparables produced a median valuation of $2.0B, though the peer set exhibits substantial dispersion (range $529M to $5.0B), reflecting heterogeneity in market positioning or investor expectations within the segment.\n\nTriangulation of these two methods supports a valuation range of $650M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median implied value of $1.4B. The wide dispersion between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects material uncertainty around relative positioning versus peers. Key sensitivities include Axelera's progress on product differentiation within the crowded AI inference chip market and the sustainability of valuation levels in the peer set, particularly the $5.0B anchor represented by Etched.",
