      "narrative": "iQPS is a publicly listed Space & Aerospace company founded by Tetsuo Yasaka, Akira Sakurai, and Kunihiro Funakoshi. The valuation universe comprises 5 public comps (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including Planet Labs, Astroscale, SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Impulse Space, totaling 13 comparable entities in the sector.\n\nTwo standard triangulation methods were evaluated. Peer-Median analysis proved inapplicable: while 11 same-sector peers exist in Space & Aerospace, the narrow filters (same stage, adjacent stage, similar valuation tier) yielded fewer than 3 datapoints in each category, falling short of the minimum threshold required for reliable median estimation. Public-Comp Anchoring was also inapplicable due to absence of target revenue data on file; though the public Space & Aerospace cohort trades at a 23.9x median P/S across 6 tickers, iQPS's revenue figures are not disclosed, precluding revenue multiple application.\n\nGiven the constraints, no triangulated valuation range can be supported by the quantitative methods available. The primary uncertainty is disclosure: iQPS's revenue, EBITDA, and other fundamental metrics are required to anchor either peer multiples or DCF frameworks. Until such financials enter the public record, valuation relies on market price discovery rather than comparable analysis. Practitioners should prioritize obtaining iQPS's disclosed financials before re-attempting peer or multiple-based valuation.",
