      "narrative": "EX-Fusion is a Series A nuclear energy company founded by Kazuki Matsuo, Shinsuke Fujioka, and Yoshitaka Mori, having raised $37M to date. The broader nuclear energy sector comprises 3 public comparables (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private peers including Fuse Energy, X-Energy, and Nano Nuclear Energy. However, the narrow peer set\u2014same-stage or adjacent-stage companies of similar valuation tier\u2014contains insufficient datapoints (fewer than 3) to support a reliable median-multiple approach.\n\nGiven this constraint, stage-progression analysis serves as the primary valuation method. Using total capital raised ($37M) as a base proxy and applying a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier associated with Series A to subsequent-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $74M. This method assumes EX-Fusion will track typical venture capital step-up patterns as it advances, a reasonable assumption for a funded frontier-tech company but one lacking sector-specific validation.\n\nThe analysis triangulates to a median of $74M, with a range of $63M (low) to $85M (high) reflecting \u00b115% variance around the point estimate. The principal uncertainties are the absence of narrow-set peer multiples\u2014precluding cross-check against sector-specific value inflection points\u2014and dependence on a single methodological pillar. Investors should supplement this analysis with technology risk assessment and competitive positioning within the nuclear energy landscape.",
