      "narrative": "NordSpace is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Rahul Goel that has raised $38M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a sector landscape comprising 6 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the primary applicable method given data constraints. Using total capital raised ($38M) as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage progression yields $76M. This method is grounded in observed venture capital step-up patterns but relies on the assumption that NordSpace's cost of capital and growth trajectory align with stage norms.\n\nPublic-comp anchoring cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures. The Space & Aerospace sector median P/S of 23.9x across five public tickers (23.90x multiple) establishes a reference frame but remains inaccessible without target-level revenue data. Peer-median analysis is similarly inapplicable; while 11 same-sector private comparables exist, the narrow filters (same-stage, adjacent-stage, similar valuation tier) yield insufficient datapoints for statistical reliability.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $65M to $87M, centered on $76M. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, capital efficiency relative to peer benchmarks, and stage-specific multiples in a sector where public and private valuation spreads remain wide. A single-method conclusion warrants material haircut relative to multi-method triangulation confidence.",
