      "narrative": "Simera Sense is a Series B stage company in Space & Aerospace that has raised $16.3M+ to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers operating in the same sector and adjacent funding stages, including Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Varda Space Industries, Aalyria, and Skyryse.\n\nTwo methodologies proved applicable. The stage-progression method, using total capital raised as a proxy base, applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yielding $31M. The peer-median approach anchors to the median valuation of five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables at $1.5B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public comparables could not be deployed due to the absence of disclosed revenue data for the target company.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $26M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $765M. This wide dispersion reflects material stage and maturity heterogeneity within the peer set. The stage-progression method floors the range at early-stage fundamentals; the peer-median anchors to later-stage private valuations. Key uncertainties include unit economics, revenue trajectory, capital intensity of future rounds, and differentiation relative to well-capitalized incumbents in the Space & Aerospace sector.",
