      "narrative": "CubeSpace is a growth-stage company in Space & Aerospace founded by Mike-Alec Kearney, Willem Jordaan, and Jako Gerber. The valuation universe comprises 13 sector peers: 5 public companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private firms including SpaceX, Sierra Space, Planet Labs, Impulse Space, and Apex Space.\n\nTwo standard triangulation methods are not applicable to this analysis. Peer-median valuation cannot be derived: while 11 same-sector peers exist, none satisfy narrow filtering criteria (same stage, adjacent stage, or similar valuation tier), and applying an all-sector median would introduce unacceptable bias. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples also cannot be calculated; the Space & Aerospace public median P/S is 23.9x across the 6-ticker set, but CubeSpace's revenue is not on file. Private companies at growth stage rarely disclose revenue, rendering this multiple inapplicable.\n\nGiven the absence of reliable quantitative inputs and the insufficiency of comparable peer data at CubeSpace's stage and tier, a valuation range cannot be supported by the available data. The key uncertainty is revenue disclosure: without top-line figures, neither relative-value methods nor multiples-based approaches can be credibly applied. Further diligence on CubeSpace's financial performance and a more granular peer-stage taxonomy would be necessary to anchor a defensible valuation.",
