      "narrative": "Constellr is a Series A space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac37M to date. The valuation universe comprises 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, Planet Labs, Impulse Space, and Apex Space\u2014a total of 13 reference points across the sector.\n\nStandard triangulation methods face material constraints here. Peer-median valuation is inapplicable: while 11 same-sector peers exist, none satisfy minimum thresholds for stage-aligned or valuation-tier-aligned groupings (the methodology requires \u22653 datapoints per bucket; zero same-stage and only two adjacent-stage peers were identified). Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiple is likewise unavailable, as Constellr's revenue is not on file\u2014typical for early-stage private companies. The Space & Aerospace public median trades at 23.9x sales across the 6-ticker universe, but without disclosed revenue, this multiple cannot be applied to derive a target valuation.\n\nThe analysis therefore reaches no quantitative range. A credible valuation would require either: disclosed or modeled Constellr revenue (to anchor the 23.9x public multiple), or identification of additional private peers with disclosed post-money valuations at identical or adjacent funding stages. The \u20ac37M raised to date provides a floor on deployment but does not establish enterprise value. Further diligence on comparable funding rounds and revenue guidance is necessary to triangulate a defensible valuation range.",
