      "narrative": "Theion is a Series A-stage frontier climate and energy company that has raised \u20ac25M+. The valuation universe comprises nine peers across the Climate & Energy sector: one public company (Lnza) and eight private firms including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen. These represent a reasonable reference class for early-stage deep tech in decarbonization, though direct stage and valuation-tier overlap remains limited.\n\nStandard peer-median triangulation is not applicable here. The Climate & Energy sector contains only nine comparable companies overall, and filtering for same-stage or adjacent-stage peers yields fewer than three datapoints\u2014the minimum threshold for reliable median-based valuation. Applying an all-sector median would introduce material bias and obscure rather than clarify fair value. The absence of tighter peer clustering reflects the nascent and heterogeneous nature of frontier energy technologies, where business models, capital intensity, and commercialization timelines vary substantially across the competitive set.\n\nThis analysis therefore cannot support a single point valuation or narrow range. Key uncertainties driving fair value include the pace and cost profile of Theion's core technology development, competitive positioning relative to the named peer group, and capital efficiency relative to peers' burn profiles. A credible range would require either additional institutional datapoints from secondary transactions or forward-looking modeling of unit economics and funding rounds. Current data is sufficient only to contextualize Theion within the frontier climate landscape, not to triangulate valuation.",
