      "narrative": "Neustark is a Series B climate and energy company that has raised $70M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a peer universe of nine private companies and one public comparable (Lnza), all operating in frontier climate and energy technology.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy for current value and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B progression, implies a valuation of $133M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014KoBold Metals ($3.0B Series C), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B Series C), and Amogy ($700M Series C)\u2014yields a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range of $700M to $3.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce materially different signals, reflecting the inherent dispersion in frontier-tech valuations. Triangulating across both approaches yields a valuation range of $113M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $566M. The wide spread reflects uncertainty in comparable company selection, stage-adjustment calibration, and the early-stage, capital-intensive nature of climate technology. Key uncertainties include technological maturity relative to peer set, unit economics trajectory, and the timing of near-term capital requirements.",
