      "narrative": "Manastu Space is a Series A-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Tushar Jadhav and Ashtesh Kumar that has raised $6M to date. The valuation universe comprises 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs, though the private peer set lacks sufficient same-stage clustering for robust median analysis.\n\nOf three triangulation methods tested, only Stage-Progression proved applicable. This method applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to next-stage transitions, anchored to the $6M total raised as a proxy for post-money valuation. This yields an implied valuation of $12M. Public-Comp Anchoring cannot be applied due to lack of disclosed revenue data\u2014a common constraint in private companies\u2014though the Space & Aerospace sector median P/S of 23.9x across the 6 public tickers establishes a reference frame. Peer-Median analysis was inapplicable; the broader Space & Aerospace universe contains 11 peers, but none of the narrow filters (same-stage, adjacent-stage, similar-tier) produced the minimum 3 datapoints required for statistical credibility.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $10M\u2013$14M, with a median point of $12M. This range reflects stage-appropriate step-up multiples applied to capital raised. Key uncertainties include revenue scale, technology differentiation within the Space & Aerospace sector, and capital efficiency relative to adjacent-stage peers, all of which remain unquantified in the dataset.",
