      "narrative": "Kneron is a Series B semiconductor company that has raised $190M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 11 firms spanning chips and semiconductors\u20143 public (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers at Series A through Series C, including SambaNova Systems ($11.0B), Etched ($5.0B), d-Matrix ($2.0B), Positron AI ($1.0B), and DEEPX ($529M).\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply to this stage and sector. Stage-progression analysis uses the $190M total raised as a proxy base and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B progression, yielding $361M. Peer-median analysis across the five sampled same-sector and same/adjacent-stage comparables produces a median valuation of $2.0B, with a range spanning $529M to $11.0B. The median peer valuation reflects heterogeneity in the sample, particularly the wide gap between earlier-stage SambaNova at $11.0B and later-stage DEEPX at $529M.\n\nTriangulating both methods yields a valuation range of $307M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.2B. The stage-progression method produces a tighter, lower-end estimate anchored to deployment capital, while peer-median reflects the broader market pricing for semiconductor infrastructure firms. Key uncertainties include technology differentiation relative to the peer set and near-term revenue trajectory, both of which will materially influence positioning within this range.",
