      "narrative": "SambaNova Systems, a Series A semiconductor company, is valued at $11.0B post-money after raising $1.1B to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 11 comparable companies across chips and semiconductors\u20143 public (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private entities including Cerebras, PsiQuantum, Etched, Tenstorrent, and Rebellions.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression approach applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A advancement to the $11.0B base valuation, implying $22.0B at the next funding round. The peer-median method examines 6 same-sector comparables, yielding a median valuation of $3.9B, though the peer set exhibits wide dispersion (range: $2.3B to $39.2B), reflecting material stage and business-model heterogeneity within frontier chip development.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $3.3B (low) to $25.3B (high), with a median of $12.9B. The current $11.0B post-money valuation sits near the midpoint of this range, suggesting reasonable calibration against peer progression dynamics. Key uncertainties include the timing and trajectory of revenue inflection for frontier chip architectures, stage-specific valuation dispersion among private peers, and the degree to which public comps (notably Cerebras at $39.2B) reflect sustainable market value versus speculative positioning. Stage-agnostic peer comparisons carry elevated uncertainty given the diversity of development timelines across the cohort.",
