      "narrative": "Credo Semiconductor is a publicly listed semiconductor company valued at approximately $35.8B following its 2022 IPO. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 3 same-sector, same-stage public comparables in Chips & Semiconductors: Cerebras ($39.2B), Ouster ($2.3B), and Aeva Technologies ($1.1B).\n\nThe peer-median method yields an implied valuation of $2.3B, representing the median across the three public comparables. The peer range spans from $1.1B at the low end to $39.2B at the high end, reflecting material dispersion within the semiconductor public market. Given the single-method constraint and three-company sample, the triangulated range is bounded at $1.9B (low), $2.3B (median), and $2.6B (high).\n\nCredo's current $35.8B market valuation sits substantially above both the peer median and the triangulated range, a gap attributable to factors not captured in peer multiples alone\u2014including revenue scale, profitability profile, or market-specific positioning relative to the three comparables selected. Key uncertainties include the limited peer sample size (n=3), the wide dispersion across comparables (35x range), and the lack of revenue or earnings multiples to anchor the analysis. A more granular valuation would require either additional comparable companies or fundamental metrics tied to growth and profitability.",
