      "narrative": "Scout Space, founded by Eric Ingram and Sergio Gallucci, is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $18M to date. The valuation universe comprises 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs, though a sufficiently sized narrow peer cohort at identical stage and valuation tier is not available for direct median benchmarking.\n\nGiven data constraints, stage-progression methodology is the sole applicable triangulation approach. Using total capital raised ($18M) as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement yields an implied valuation of $36M. This reflects the expected value accretion between Series A close and subsequent financing rounds. Public Space & Aerospace comparables trade at a median P/S multiple of 23.9x across six tickers; however, Scout Space's revenue is not disclosed, precluding revenue-based anchoring.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $31M to $41M (median $36M), derived from sensitivity around the stage-progression base case. Key uncertainties include the absence of Scout Space-specific financial metrics, limited same-stage private peer data, and inability to apply public market multiples without revenue disclosure. Any refinement would require either comparable transaction data from the narrow Space & Aerospace venture set or disclosure of target revenue figures for public multiple triangulation.",
