      "narrative": "Thea Energy is a Series B nuclear energy company founded by Brian Berzin that has raised $137M+ to date. The valuation exercise draws from a comp universe of 11 total peers across nuclear energy\u20143 public (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms including Oklo, X-Energy, Nano Nuclear Energy, Fuse Energy, and Aalo Atomics.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method is applicable here and serves as the primary triangulation anchor. Using $100M as a proxy for total capital raised and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement yields an implied valuation of $190M. The Peer-Median approach is not applicable; while four same-sector peers exist, the narrow filtering criteria (same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar valuation tier) yielded fewer than three comparable datapoints, making a median calculation unreliable and sector-wide medians potentially misleading given stage and business-model heterogeneity.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $162M (low) to $218M (high), with a median of $190M. This range reflects the single-method foundation and the typical dispersion around stage-progression estimates. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the 1.9x multiplier for advanced nuclear sub-segments, the composition of the $137M+ raised (seed vs. Series A vs. Series B allocation), and whether comparable companies' capital efficiency meaningfully differs from Thea Energy's deployment model.",
