      "narrative": "BRINC Drones, a Series C defense and security drone manufacturer founded by Blake Resnick, has raised $157M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of 12 same-sector and adjacent-stage companies, including 2 public comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms such as Quantum-Systems, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic.\n\nTwo triangulation methods support the valuation range. Stage-progression methodology applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $157M raised proxy, yielding $267M. Peer-median analysis across the 12-company cohort produces $1.8B, with the peer set spanning $300M to $18.0B; notable comparables include Quantum-Systems at $8.0B (Series C), Helsing at $18.0B (Series D), and Chaos Industries at $4.5B (Series D). The wide peer dispersion reflects heterogeneity in company maturity, customer concentration, and technical differentiation within the frontier defense tech segment.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $227M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $1.0B. The gap between stage-progression ($267M) and peer-median ($1.8B) reflects material uncertainty regarding BRINC's competitive positioning relative to better-capitalized peers and its path to larger defense contracts. Key sensitivities include customer concentration, regulatory clearances, and actual revenue scale relative to the peer set's heterogeneous traction profiles.",
