      "narrative": "Performance Drone Works is a Series B autonomous systems company that has raised $110M+ to date. The broader Drones & Autonomous sector comprises eight private peers including Elroy Air, Zipline, Joby Aviation, Nuro, and Archer Aviation, with no direct public comparables available for valuation anchoring.\n\nStage-progression methodology is applicable here and forms the sole quantitative input to the valuation. Using total capital raised of $110M as a baseline proxy and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement yields an implied valuation of $209M. This approach reflects the expectation that enterprise value expands materially between Series B and subsequent funding rounds, though it relies on the assumption that the company's capital efficiency and market conditions align with historical norms for the sector.\n\nPeer-median analysis is not applicable due to insufficient comparable data: while five same-sector companies exist, none yielded three or more datapoints meeting narrow filters for stage, timing, or valuation tier. A broader cross-sector median would introduce unacceptable noise and has been rejected.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $178M (low) to $240M (high), centered on $209M. The primary uncertainty stems from reliance on a single methodology and the absence of transaction comparables in the narrow peer set. Resolution of valuation range would benefit from additional Series B stage transactions in autonomous systems or expanded disclosure of capital efficiency metrics across the five identified peers.",
