      "narrative": "Deep Sentinel, a Series B defense and security company that has raised $55M to date, is evaluated against a comparables universe of 10 peers spanning 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private entities operating in the same sector.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applied. The stage-progression approach, using total capital raised as a proxy baseline, applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $104M. The peer-median method examines 7 same-sector, same-stage comparables including Dream Security ($3.0B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), Castelion ($1.0B), and Defense Unicorns ($1.0B), with a median valuation of $1.0B and a range spanning $300M to $3.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across these two methods produces a valuation range of $89M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $552M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty in how Deep Sentinel's stage and capital efficiency compare to a peer set exhibiting significant valuation heterogeneity. Stage-progression suggests a tighter, lower-end estimate anchored to observed fundraising, while peer-median reflects sector-wide valuations but risks overstating comparability if Deep Sentinel's technology differentiation, customer traction, or capital efficiency diverges materially from sampled peers. Key uncertainties center on revenue metrics, customer concentration, and regulatory pathway clarity within defense verticals.",
