      "narrative": "LuxWall, founded by Scott Thomsen, is a Series B-stage Climate & Energy company that has raised $84M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a peer universe of 9 private companies and 1 public comparable (LNZA), all operating in frontier energy and materials technology.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The Stage-Progression method uses the $84M total raised as a baseline proxy and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $160M. The Peer-Median method benchmarks against three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: KoBold Metals ($3.0B Series C), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B Series C), and Amogy ($700M Series C). The median of this peer set is $1.0B, with a range from $700M to $3.0B, reflecting heterogeneity in maturity and capital intensity within the Climate & Energy frontier segment.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $136M (low), $580M (median), and $1.1B (high). The Stage-Progression method anchors the lower bound, while the Peer-Median approach dominates the upper range. The substantial spread between low and high reflects material uncertainty around LuxWall's relative progress against peers and the volatility in late-stage Climate & Energy valuations. Key sensitivities include the company's differentiation within the peer cohort and the sustainability of recent funding multiples in this sector.",
