      "narrative": "Cambium, a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by Simon Waddington and Stephan Herrera, has raised $127M+ to date. Valuation analysis draws on two primary methods triangulated against a peer set of four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies (Bedrock Robotics at $1.8B, Dexterity at $1.6B, Hadrian at $1.6B, and Nimble Robotics at $1.0B), supplemented by one public comparable.\n\nStage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $127M total raised proxy, yielding $241M. Peer-median analysis across the four robotics comparables produces $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $1.8B. These two methods reflect different assumptions about capital efficiency and market positioning relative to peers.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $205M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $933M. The 9.4x spread between low and high estimates reflects material uncertainty around Cambium's positioning relative to better-capitalized Series B/C cohort peers. Key variables include capital efficiency relative to the peer set, revenue or product traction metrics not provided in this data, and stage-specific risk pricing. The peer-median method carries higher weight given direct comparability, though confidence remains constrained by limited visibility into Cambium's operational performance.",
