      "narrative": "Fulfil is a Series B-stage robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $127M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparables universe of 9 private and 1 public peer in the robotics sector, including same-stage companies like Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B) and Dexterity ($1.6B), as well as adjacent-stage peers Hadrian and Nimble Robotics.\n\nTwo triangulation methods prove applicable. The stage-progression method applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $127M total raised, implying a valuation of $241M. The peer-median method calculates the median across the four comparable companies at $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $1.8B. This wider band reflects the heterogeneity inherent in same/adjacent-stage comparables across the robotics sector.\n\nThe triangulated analysis yields a low estimate of $205M, a median of $933M, and a high of $1.9B. The significant dispersion between methods reflects tension between capital-based valuation anchors and peer transaction multiples. The stage-progression method produces a more conservative floor, while peer-median evidence suggests the market has valued comparable Series B/C robotics businesses substantially higher. Key uncertainties include revenue metrics relative to peers, technology differentiation within the fulfillment robotics subsector, and whether Fulfil's capital efficiency exceeds or lags the comparables set. A valuation range of $600M\u2013$1.3B may better reflect material data risk than the full triangulated bounds.",
