      "narrative": "JITX is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $12M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 9 private companies and 1 public company in the robotics and manufacturing sector, including peers such as Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B, Seed).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy for post-money value, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to next-stage progression, implying a valuation of $24M. Peer-median analysis relies on three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with a median valuation of $1.6B and a range spanning $1.1B to $1.8B, implying $1.6B. The wide dispersion between these methods reflects the methodological tension between bootstrapping from capital raised versus anchoring to later-stage peer outcomes.\n\nThe triangulated analysis yields a range of $20M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $837M. This wide band reflects material uncertainty around JITX's positioning within the peer set and the applicability of later-stage comparable valuations to an early Series A company. Key sensitivities include product maturity relative to Series B peers and revenue traction, neither of which are available in this dataset. A narrower range would require data on revenue, unit economics, or explicit stage-adjusted multiples.",
