      "narrative": "ISEE, a Series B drone and autonomous systems company founded by Yibiao Zhao, has raised $70M to date. The broader Drones & Autonomous sector comprises 8 private peers including Elroy Air, Zipline, Joby Aviation, Nuro, and Archer Aviation, with no public comparables available for direct benchmarking.\n\nValuation analysis is constrained by limited comparable data. The Peer-Median method was not applicable due to insufficient narrow-stage peer density\u2014only one same-stage peer exists in the filtered set, below the three-point minimum required for statistical reliability. Consequently, the Stage-Progression method provides the primary anchor, applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $70M total capital raised as a proxy baseline. This approach yields an implied valuation of $133M, reflecting typical venture funding progression for Series B advancement.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $113M (low) to $153M (high), centered at $133M. This narrow band reflects reliance on a single methodology rather than true triangulation across independent approaches. Key uncertainties include the absence of public market comparables, limited private peer visibility at ISEE's specific stage and tier, and lack of operational metrics (revenue, growth rate, unit economics) to stress-test the stage-based assumption. A more robust valuation would require either disclosure of additional same-stage comparable financials or operational data from ISEE itself.",
