      "narrative": "Mojo Vision is a Series B semiconductor company founded by Drew Perkins and Michael Wiemer that has raised $345M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 5 private companies in the Chips & Semiconductors sector at same or adjacent stages, supplemented by 3 public semiconductor comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD). The private peer universe includes Positron AI ($1.0B, Series B), d-Matrix ($2.0B, Series C), Etched ($5.0B, Series C), SambaNova Systems ($11.0B, Series A), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. The stage-progression method applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $345M raised proxy, implying $656M. The peer-median method across the 5-company cohort yields a median valuation of $2.0B, with a range spanning $529M to $11.0B. The peer sample reflects considerable dispersion, reflecting variance in capital efficiency and market timing within the segment.\n\nTriangulating across both methods produces a valuation range of $557M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.3B. The stage-progression method anchors the lower bound, while peer-median anchors the mid-to-upper range. Key uncertainties include the composition sensitivity of the peer set\u2014the $11.0B SambaNova outlier drives median elevation\u2014and whether Mojo Vision's capital efficiency and technical positioning align with median-stage peers or the lower-cost outliers within the set.",
