      "narrative": "Electra.aero is a Series B transportation company founded by John Langford that has raised $235M to date. The valuation universe for comparison consists of seven private frontier-transport companies including Rivian, The Boring Company, Einride, Arc Boats, and The ePlane Company. No public comparables exist in this narrow subsector, limiting conventional multiples-based approaches.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method is the primary applicable valuation approach, applying a 1.9x multiplier to the $235M raised proxy to reflect typical value creation from Series B to subsequent rounds. This yields an implied valuation of $446M. A peer-median approach could not be applied: while three transportation companies exist in the broader comp universe, zero same-stage and zero adjacent-stage matches met minimum thresholds (\u22653 datapoints required), making sector-wide medians unreliable for this specific company profile.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $380M (low) to $513M (high), with a median of $446M. This range reflects stage-based progression norms but carries meaningful uncertainty given reliance on a single methodology. Key sensitivities include: (1) scarcity of direct Series B\u2013stage comparables in frontier transportation, (2) lack of public-market anchors for the subsector, and (3) company-specific execution risk not captured in stage-progression mechanics. Additional data on comparable Series B exit multiples or later-stage fundraising activity for peer companies would strengthen conviction in this range.",
