      "narrative": "Project Omega, a Seed-stage nuclear energy company founded by Stafford Sheehan, has raised $12M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a broader nuclear energy comp universe of 11 peers (3 public, 8 private), including companies such as Oklo, Nano Nuclear Energy, X-Energy, Fuse Energy, and Applied Atomics.\n\nA Stage-Progression methodology is the primary applicable valuation tool here. Using the $12M total capital raised as a proxy base value and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of progression from Seed to the next stage yields an implied valuation of $30M. A Peer-Median approach could not be reliably applied due to insufficient narrow-stage comparables within nuclear energy\u2014while four same-sector peers exist, filtering to same-stage or adjacent-stage companies yielded fewer than three datapoints, making a sector-median approach potentially misleading rather than informative.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $26M to $34M, with a median of $30M. This single-method result reflects meaningful uncertainty: the analysis lacks the anchoring power of multiple independent valuation approaches. Key risks to this range include the early-stage nature of nuclear technology commercialization, regulatory pathway clarity, and the sparse peer dataset in this subsector. Any forward revision would benefit substantially from additional comparable transactions or revenue/development milestones that could support alternative methodologies.",
