      "narrative": "Star Catcher, a Space & Aerospace company at Series A stage, has raised $88M to date. The valuation universe consists of 13 total comparables: 5 public companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs. However, the narrow peer set\u2014no same-stage Series A comps with sufficient data density\u2014constrains methodological options.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the sole applicable method. Using total raised ($88M) as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A-to-subsequent-stage advancement yields $176M. Public-comp anchoring cannot be deployed: the Space & Aerospace sector median trading multiple is 23.9x across 6 public tickers, but Star Catcher's revenue is undisclosed, preventing P/S application. Peer-median triangulation was not viable given insufficient same-or-adjacent-stage private comparables meeting minimum thresholds (0 same-stage, 2 adjacent-stage identified; minimum 3 required).\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $150M to $202M, with $176M as the point estimate. This reflects a conservative 1.7x to 2.3x uplift from capital raised. Key uncertainties include: the absence of revenue metrics to anchor against public multiples, limited comparable transaction data at this stage in the Space & Aerospace sector, and the target's product maturity relative to private peers. Further refinement would require disclosure of financial metrics or closer engagement with private round pricing history.",
