      "narrative": "Swan is a Seed-stage defense and security company founded by Dima Kislovskiy and Narek Melik Barkhudarov that has raised $38.5M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comparables universe of 10 peers\u20142 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic\u2014all operating in the same sector at Seed or Series A stage.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $38.5M raised as a proxy for current value and applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage transitions, yielding $96M. Peer-median valuation draws on three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (UFORCE at $1.0B, Singularity at $400M, NODA AI at $125M), producing a median of $400M and a range of $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThese methods triangulate to a valuation range of $82M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $248M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty around Swan's position within the defense tech market: the gap between stage-progression and peer-median approaches suggests sensitivity to whether Swan's capital efficiency and growth trajectory more closely resemble early-stage funding patterns or the later-stage metrics of better-capitalized competitors. Public market comparables and relative revenue multiples\u2014where available\u2014would narrow this range.",
