      "narrative": "Onebrief, a Series D defense and security technology company founded by Grant Demaree and Rafa Pereira, is evaluated against a universe of 10 comparable companies: 8 private firms and 2 public equities (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS). The peer set for same-stage, same-sector analysis comprises Helsing ($18.0B), Saronic ($9.2B), and Chaos Industries ($4.5B).\n\nTwo valuation methods yield distinct but complementary signals. The stage-progression approach applies a 1.5x step-up multiplier to Onebrief's last post-money valuation of $2.1B, implying $3.2B. The peer-median method anchors to the three same-sector, same-stage comparables, producing a median valuation of $9.2B with a range spanning $4.5B to $18.0B. The peer set reflects material dispersion, with the highest comparable (Helsing) trading at 4.0x the lowest (Chaos Industries).\n\nTriangulating these methods yields a valuation range of $2.7B to $10.6B, with a median of $6.2B. Onebrief's current $2.15B post-money sits at the lower bound, suggesting upside under peer-relative framing. Key uncertainties center on which comparable best reflects Onebrief's competitive positioning and growth trajectory within the defense tech segment, and whether peer valuations reflect sustainable market dynamics or sector exuberance.",
