      "narrative": "Vermeer is a Series A-stage Defense & Security company that has raised $10M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 10 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables, comprising 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, Singularity, and NODA AI.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $10M raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A progression, implies a $20M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the 10-company comparable set yields a $1.0B median valuation, with a range spanning $125M to $3.0B. The peer sample includes Dream Security at $3.0B (Series B), Harmattan AI at $1.4B, Code Metal at $1.2B, and Castelion and Defense Unicorns both at $1.0B.\n\nTriangulating these methods yields a valuation range of $17M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $510M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty regarding Vermeer's product maturity, commercial traction, and capital efficiency relative to the peer set. Stage-progression alone appears understated given peer valuations; however, peer comparables may not fully adjust for early-stage risk or differentiated technology. Resolution of product-market fit and revenue trajectory will be critical to narrowing this range.",
