      "narrative": "Nth Cycle, a growth-stage climate and energy company founded by Megan O'Connor and Chad Vecitis, has raised $60M in equity alongside a $1.1B 10-year offtake agreement with Trafigura. The valuation exercise draws from a fragmented comp universe: one public company (LNZA) and eight private peers including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen.\n\nStandard peer-median valuation proved inapplicable here. The Climate & Energy sector contains nine total public and private comparables, but filtering for same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar valuation-tier companies yielded fewer than three datapoints in any narrow category\u2014below the minimum threshold for reliable triangulation. A full-sector median would conflate companies across materially different growth phases and scales, introducing substantial noise rather than signal.\n\nThe absence of tightly aligned comps reflects a real characteristic of the frontier-tech climate sector: heterogeneity in technology, capital requirements, and path to revenue. Without sufficient peer clustering, traditional multiples-based valuation lacks defensibility. Any forward valuation estimate for Nth Cycle would require either (1) a longer time horizon allowing more comparable exits and public offerings to mature, or (2) discounted cash flow analysis anchored to the Trafigura offtake terms\u2014the one contractual floor in the dataset. The offtake provides rare downside clarity in an otherwise sparse comparable landscape.",
