      "narrative": "TerraFirma, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $115M to date, was valued using triangulation across a comparable universe of 9 private and 1 public peer company. The private peer set includes Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, and Locus Robotics, spanning seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $115M total raised as a proxy for post-money value and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implies a valuation of $230M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B, Seed)\u2014yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range of $1.1B to $1.8B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $196M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $940M. The significant spread reflects inherent stage and growth-trajectory uncertainty within the peer set: stage-progression anchors conservatively to capital deployed, while peer-median reflects the elevated valuations of later-stage robotics companies. Key uncertainties include TerraFirma's revenue generation relative to peers, the specific technology differentiation relative to Bedrock and Dexterity, and whether later-stage peer multiples appropriately reflect Series A risk and stage.",
