      "narrative": "ForSight Robotics is a Series B biotech & health company that has raised $195M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comp universe of 11 peers: 3 public companies (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private firms spanning the same sector and stage band, with particular focus on Eikon Therapeutics ($539M Series B), Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B Series C), Chai Discovery ($3.8B Series C), and New Limit ($3.1B Series C).\n\nTwo quantitative methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, anchored to the $195M cumulative raise as a valuation proxy, applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $370M. Peer-median triangulation across the four comparable companies produces a $3.5B implied valuation, with the full peer range spanning $539M to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (5.6x median across the three public tickers) cannot be applied absent the target's disclosed revenue.\n\nThe two-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $315M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.9B. The wide dispersion reflects genuine uncertainty: stage-progression yields a conservative floor given limited revenue visibility at Series B, while peer medians reflect the volatility inherent in biotech valuations at growth stages. Key unknowns include ForSight's revenue trajectory, clinical progress, and IP defensibility relative to the peer set.",
